455>>>>>>>>>
455>>>>>>>>>// This command maps a character to a virtual key code and shift state.
455>>>>>>>>>//
455>>>>>>>>>//      1st Parameter is the char to translate. Integer represents TCHAR.
455>>>>>>>>>//      2nd Parameter is the virtual key code and shift state.
455>>>>>>>>>//        If the function succeeds, the low-order byte of the return value contains the virtual-key code
455>>>>>>>>>//    and the high-order byte contains the shift state, which can be a combination of the following flag
455>>>>>>>>>//    bits:
455>>>>>>>>>//
455>>>>>>>>>//Bit  1 Meaning  Either SHIFT key is pressed.
455>>>>>>>>>//     2 Either CTRL key is pressed.
455>>>>>>>>>//     4 Either ALT key is pressed.
455>>>>>>>>>//
455>>>>>>>>>//        If the function finds no key that translates to the passed character code, both the low-order
455>>>>>>>>>//    and high-order bytes contain -1.
455>>>>>>>>>//
