613>>>>>>>>>>>// Windows structs used by the packages. We use the prefix tWin for all of these structs. Therefore we
613>>>>>>>>>>>// discourage developers from using this same prefix method. If you need to create you own windows structs
613>>>>>>>>>>>// use some other naming convention. This avoids the possibility of conflicts where the same struct was
613>>>>>>>>>>>// defined twice. Using a #IFDEF to check for this is not recommended because the defintions might differ.
