5404>>>>>>>
5404>>>>>>>    // The following messages are used to control smart file mode exception
5404>>>>>>>    // handling. The message "Send Add_system_File file# Fg" allows you to
5404>>>>>>>    // add system files (or any other files not known to the dso structure)
5404>>>>>>>    // within define_fields. This allows you to not have to augment the msg
5404>>>>>>>    // reset_filemodes_for_lock. The only truly public messages here are
5404>>>>>>>    // Add_system_file and Remove_system_File (which s/b rarely used).
5404>>>>>>>
5404>>>>>>>    // Adds a system file for smart_file_mode handling. A second optional
5404>>>>>>>    // parameter may be passed to determine of the sys file should only be
5404>>>>>>>    // locked during a new save (and not during a delete or a save of an
5404>>>>>>>    // existing record). It is expected that this will be the only public
5404>>>>>>>    // message used to control smart filemode. All of the remaining sys file
5404>>>>>>>    // messages are considered advanced.
5404>>>>>>>    Procedure Add_System_File Integer iFile Integer iLock_Mode
5406>>>>>>>        Integer iobj iCnt iMode
5406>>>>>>>        If (Num_arguments = 1) ;            Move DD_Lock_on_All to iMode
5409>>>>>>>        Else ;            Move iLock_Mode     to iMode
5411>>>>>>>        Move (system_file_obj(Self)) to iObj
5412>>>>>>>        Get Item_Count  of iObj to iCnt
5413>>>>>>>        Set Array_Value of iObj iCnt to iFile
5414>>>>>>>        Increment iCnt
5415>>>>>>>        Set Array_Value of iObj iCnt to iMode
5416>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
5417>>>>>>>
5417>>>>>>>    // Return number of system files
5417>>>>>>>    Function System_File_Count Returns Integer
5419>>>>>>>        Function_Return (Item_Count(System_File_Obj(Self))/2)
5420>>>>>>>    End_Function
5421>>>>>>>
5421>>>>>>>    // Returns system file number for passed item.
5421>>>>>>>    Function System_File_Number Integer iItem Returns Integer
5423>>>>>>>        Function_Return (Integer_Value(System_File_Obj(Self),iItem*2))
5424>>>>>>>    End_Function
5425>>>>>>>
5425>>>>>>>    // Returns system flag to determine if file is only used during a new
5425>>>>>>>    // save (and not during an exiting save or a delete).
5425>>>>>>>    Function System_File_Lock_Mode Integer iItem Returns Integer
5427>>>>>>>        Function_Return (Integer_Value(System_File_Obj(Self),iItem*2+1))
5428>>>>>>>    End_Function
5429>>>>>>>
5429>>>>>>>    // Removes a system_file for smart_file_Mode handling. This remvoes the
5429>>>>>>>    // first occurance of the file (S/b the only occurance). We assume that
5429>>>>>>>    // this will be rarely used.
5429>>>>>>>    Procedure Remove_System_File Integer iFile
5431>>>>>>>        Integer iobj iCnt iItmCnt
5431>>>>>>>        Get System_file_Count to iItmCnt
5432>>>>>>>        Decrement iItmCnt
5433>>>>>>>        For iCnt from 0 to iItmCnt
5439>>>>>>>>
5439>>>>>>>            If (System_File_Number(Self,iCnt)=iFile) Begin
5441>>>>>>>                Move (system_file_obj(Self)) to iObj
5442>>>>>>>                Move (iCnt*2) to iCnt
5443>>>>>>>                Send Delete_Item to iObj iCnt
5444>>>>>>>                Send Delete_Item to iObj iCnt
5445>>>>>>>                Procedure_Return
5446>>>>>>>            End
5446>>>>>>>>
5446>>>>>>>        Loop
5447>>>>>>>>
5447>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
5448>>>>>>>
