5790>>>>>>>
5790>>>>>>>    // This returns the main index for a field. This replaces the DSO message Field_Main_index which
5790>>>>>>>    // should no longer be used by DDOs. The old message has the problem that the DDO or DSO using
5790>>>>>>>    // this message may not be the owner of the field. So augmenting the owner DDO did not insure that
5790>>>>>>>    // all requests for this index would go through it. Now you can augment Field_Index and always
5790>>>>>>>    // be sure that any DDO requesting an index for a file (via file_field_index) will always go to
5790>>>>>>>    // the owner object.
5790>>>>>>>    Function Field_Index Integer iField Returns Integer
5792>>>>>>>        Integer iFile iIndex iOrder
5792>>>>>>>        // ordering takes precendence
5792>>>>>>>        Get ordering to iOrder
5793>>>>>>>        If (iOrder>=0);            Move iOrder to iIndex  //ordering takes precedence over main index
5796>>>>>>>        Else Begin
5797>>>>>>>            Get Main_file to iFile
5798>>>>>>>            Get_Attribute DF_FIELD_INDEX of iFile iField to iIndex // main index field
5801>>>>>>>            If (iIndex=0 and iField>0) ; // If field is not recnum and there is no index, the                Move -1 to iIndex        // field has no main index
5804>>>>>>>        End
5804>>>>>>>>
5804>>>>>>>        Function_Return iIndex
5805>>>>>>>    End_Function
5806>>>>>>>
5806>>>>>>>    // In all cases, this message should be sent instead of Field_Main_Index. If
5806>>>>>>>    // augmentation was used in Field_Main_Index, use Field_Index to insure the owner object
5806>>>>>>>    // is called.
5806>>>>>>>
5806>>>>>>>    Function File_Field_Index Integer iFile Integer iField Returns Integer
5808>>>>>>>        Integer iIndex
5808>>>>>>>        Handle hoDD
5808>>>>>>>        Get Data_set iFile to hoDD
5809>>>>>>>        If (hoDD) ;            Get Field_Index of hoDD iField to iIndex
5812>>>>>>>        Else ;            Move -1 to iIndex
5814>>>>>>>        Function_Return iIndex
5815>>>>>>>    End_Function
5816>>>>>>>
5816>>>>>>>    // 12/1 change: Make sure all of the major DD operations update the DD with the value in
5816>>>>>>>    // the focus field. After the actual find, save, clar or delete, the DD buffer contains information that
5816>>>>>>>    // is not yet reflected in the DEOs (before refresh is called) we want to make sure that we
5816>>>>>>>    // don't try to get data from the DEO. Get Field_Current_Value now checks if operation_mode is
5816>>>>>>>    // non-zero. If it is, it always gets from the DD buffer.
5816>>>>>>>
5816>>>>>>>    Procedure Clear
5818>>>>>>>        Boolean bOpOk
5818>>>>>>>        Move (OPERATION_MODE=MODE_WAITING or OPERATION_MODE=MODE_VALIDATING) to bOpOk
5819>>>>>>>        If (OPERATION_MODE=MODE_WAITING) Begin
5821>>>>>>>            Send Update_Focus_Field_For_Operation MODE_CLEARING
5822>>>>>>>        End
5822>>>>>>>>
5822>>>>>>>        If (bOpOk) Begin
5824>>>>>>>            Send OnPreFind DDFindClear
5825>>>>>>>        End
5825>>>>>>>>
5825>>>>>>>        Forward Send Clear
5827>>>>>>>        If (bOpOk) Begin
5829>>>>>>>            Send DefaultParentAutofinds
5830>>>>>>>            Send OnPostFind DDFindClear True
5831>>>>>>>        End
5831>>>>>>>>
5831>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
5832>>>>>>>
5832>>>>>>>    Procedure Clear_All
5834>>>>>>>        Boolean bOpOk
5834>>>>>>>        Move (OPERATION_MODE=MODE_WAITING or OPERATION_MODE=MODE_VALIDATING) to bOpOk
5835>>>>>>>        If (OPERATION_MODE=MODE_WAITING) Begin
5837>>>>>>>            Send Update_Focus_Field_For_Operation MODE_CLEARINGALL
5838>>>>>>>        End
5838>>>>>>>>
5838>>>>>>>        Forward Send clear_all
5840>>>>>>>        If (bOpOk) Begin
5842>>>>>>>            Send DefaultParentAutofinds
5843>>>>>>>        End
5843>>>>>>>>
5843>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
