14097>>>>>>>>>Class cFileIdsSet is a Set
14098>>>>>>>>>    // Set object will contain File Names
14098>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Construct_Object
14100>>>>>>>>>        Forward Send Construct_Object
14102>>>>>>>>>        Object oFileNr is an Array
14104>>>>>>>>>        End_Object
14105>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
14106>>>>>>>>>    
14106>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Clear_File_Data
14108>>>>>>>>>        Send Delete_Data
14109>>>>>>>>>        Send Delete_Data of oFileNr
14110>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
14111>>>>>>>>>    
14111>>>>>>>>>    Function File_Count Returns Integer
14113>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (Item_Count(Self))
14114>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
14115>>>>>>>>>    
14115>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set_File_Data String sName Integer iFileNr
14117>>>>>>>>>        Integer iCount
14117>>>>>>>>>        Move (UpperCase(sName)) to sName
14118>>>>>>>>>        Get find_element sName to iCount // search for Dups
14119>>>>>>>>>        If (iCount >= 0) ; // if found, we have an error            Error 900 (SFormat(C_$FileNameAlreadyExists, sName))
14122>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
14123>>>>>>>>>            Get File_Count to iCount
14124>>>>>>>>>            Set Value            iCount to sName
14125>>>>>>>>>            Set Value of oFileNr iCount to iFileNr
14126>>>>>>>>>        End
14126>>>>>>>>>>
14126>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
14127>>>>>>>>>    
14127>>>>>>>>>    Function File_RootName Integer iItem Returns String
14129>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (Value(Self,iItem))
14130>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
14131>>>>>>>>>    
14131>>>>>>>>>    Function File_Nr Integer iItem Returns Integer
14133>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (Value(oFileNr(Self),iItem))
14134>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
14135>>>>>>>>>    
14135>>>>>>>>>    Function Search_File_Item String sName Returns Integer
14137>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (find_element(Self, Uppercase(sName)))
14138>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
14139>>>>>>>>>    
14139>>>>>>>>>    // ret: 0 if not found, else file number of file
14139>>>>>>>>>    Function Search_File_Name String sName Returns Integer
14141>>>>>>>>>        Integer iItm
14141>>>>>>>>>        Get Search_File_Item sName to iItm // ret: -1 or item #
14142>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return ( If(iItm=-1, 0, File_nr(Self,iItm)) )
14143>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
14144>>>>>>>>>    
14144>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Initialize_Files
14146>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
14146>>>>>>>>>        String sname
14146>>>>>>>>>        Send Clear_File_Data
14147>>>>>>>>>        Move 0 to iFile
14148>>>>>>>>>        Repeat
14148>>>>>>>>>>
14148>>>>>>>>>            Get_Attribute Df_File_Next_Used of iFile to iFile
14151>>>>>>>>>            If (iFile = 0) ;                Break
14154>>>>>>>>>            Get_Attribute Df_File_Logical_Name of iFile to sName
14157>>>>>>>>>            Send Set_File_Data sName iFile
14158>>>>>>>>>        Loop
14159>>>>>>>>>>
14159>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
14160>>>>>>>>>    
14160>>>>>>>>>    // Search_Field_Name provides a way of getting the
14160>>>>>>>>>    // field Name without generating an error. We will use an error
14160>>>>>>>>>    // handle in this object to "swallow" the error.
14160>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Error_Report Integer iErrNum Integer iErrLine String sErrMsg
14162>>>>>>>>>        Move True to Err
14163>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
14164>>>>>>>>>    
14164>>>>>>>>>    Function Search_Field_Name Integer iFile String sFieldName Returns Integer
14166>>>>>>>>>        Handle hOldErr
14166>>>>>>>>>        Integer iField
14166>>>>>>>>>        If (iFile = 0) ;            Function_Return 0
14169>>>>>>>>>        Move Error_Object_id to hOldErr           // push error handler
14170>>>>>>>>>        Move Self to Error_Object_Id    // redirect here, it is silent!
14171>>>>>>>>>        Move False to Err
14172>>>>>>>>>        Field_Map iFile sFieldName to iField      // this could gen an error, we will trap it here
14174>>>>>>>>>        Move hOldErr to Error_object_id           // pop old error handler
14175>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (If( (Err), -1, iField))
14176>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
14177>>>>>>>>>    
14177>>>>>>>>>End_Class
