17716>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Server Returns Integer
17718>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer obj#
17718>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get private.Server to obj#
17719>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (obj# = 0 and Component_State(Self)) ;            Function_Return (Locate_Server(parent(Self)))
17722>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return obj#
17723>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
17724>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
17724>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
17724>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure sets the value of the Server property of this object,
17724>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   notifying child-objects of the change, and destroying and creating
17724>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   connections with database agents, as required.
17724>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
17724>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   If the Server of this object is changed while this object is inactive,
17724>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   no notification of child-objects is required or performed.
17724>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Server Integer newVal
17726>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer oldVal
17726>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set explicit_server_state to (newVal <> 0)
17727>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to oldVal
17728>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (newVal <> 0) ;            Set private.Server to (object_id(newVal))
17731>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Else ;            Set private.Server to newVal
17733>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (active_state(Self)) Begin
17735>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Broadcast Send server_changed oldVal newVal
17737>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (oldVal <> 0) ;                Send remove_deo_from_server  //detach from current server
17740>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (newval <> 0) ;                Send attach_deo_to_server    //attach to new server
17743>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
17743>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17743>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
17744>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
17744>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure servers as notification of a change in the connection
17744>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   of this object's parent to its database agent.  If this object uses
17744>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   its parent's database agent by default (see the Server and Find_Server
17744>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   functions, above), it must disconnect from the old agent and connect
17744>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   with the new agent.
17744>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure server_changed Integer oldVal Integer newVal
17746>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer oldSrvr
17746>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // as of 17.0, containers will be added as a DEO so it receives the Refresh message
17746>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get private.Server to oldSrvr
17747>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (oldSrvr = 0) Begin  //assumes Server(self) = oldVal by deleg
17749>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (oldVal <> 0) ;                Send remove_user_interface to oldVal Self
17752>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (newVal <> 0) ;                Send add_user_interface to newVal Self
17755>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
17755>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17755>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
17756>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
17756>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
17756>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure empties the Watched_Servers broadcaster, after
17756>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   detaching this object from all of the broadcaster's elements.
17756>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure is invoked by Find_Servers_to_Watch, in preparation
17756>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   for a scan. Deletes both sets of watched servers
17756>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
17756>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure delete_watched_servers
17758>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer vis#
17758>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
17758>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get watched_servers to vis#
17759>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If vis# Begin
17761>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Remove_User_Interface to vis# Self True //detach from all, TRUE for watchers
17762>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of vis# to False
17763>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send delete_Data to vis#                    //empty it
17764>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of vis# to True
17765>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
17765>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17765>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
17765>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get ChangedStateWatched_Servers to vis#
17766>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If vis# Begin
17768>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of vis# to False
17769>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send delete_Data to vis#                    //empty it
17770>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of vis# to True
17771>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
17771>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17771>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
17772>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
17772>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure adds the specified object id (obj#) to this object's
17772>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   set of database agents who are merely 'watched', and establishes a
17772>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   connection between the database agent and this object.
17772>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure add_watched_server Integer obj#
17774>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer vis# ndx
17774>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get watched_servers to vis#
17775>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // if w server does not exist, first create it
17775>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (Vis# = 0) Begin
17777>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Create of Desktop U_Broadcaster to Vis#
17778>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Watched_Servers to Vis#
17779>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
17779>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17779>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        //
17779>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set broadcast_state of vis# to False
17780>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get find_element of vis# obj# to ndx
17781>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (ndx < 0) ;            Send add_element to vis# obj#
17784>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set broadcast_state of vis# to True
17785>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (ndx lt 0 and active_State(Self)) ;            Send add_user_interface to obj# Self True // TRUE for watchers
17788>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
17789>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
17789>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure add_ChangedStateWatched_Servers Integer obj#
17791>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer vis# ndx
17791>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get ChangedStateWatched_Servers to vis#
17792>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (Vis# = 0) Begin
17794>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Create of Desktop U_Broadcaster to Vis#
17795>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set ChangedStateWatched_Servers to Vis#
17796>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
17796>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17796>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        //
17796>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set broadcast_state of vis# to False
17797>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get find_element of vis# obj# to ndx
17798>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (ndx < 0) ;            Send add_element to vis# obj#
17801>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set broadcast_state of vis# to True
17802>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
17803>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
17803>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
17803>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure removes the specified object id (obj#) from this object's
17803>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   set of database agents who are merely 'watched', and destroys the
17803>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   connection between the database agent and this object.
17803>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure remove_watched_server Integer obj#
17805>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer vis# ndx
17805>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get watched_servers to vis#
17806>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // Only if w server exists
17806>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If vis# Begin
17808>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of vis# to False
17809>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get find_element of vis# obj# to ndx
17810>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (ndx >= 0) ;                Send remove_element to vis# obj#
17813>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of vis# to True
17814>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (ndx >= 0 and active_State(Self)) ;                Send remove_user_interface to obj# Self True // TRUE for watchers
17817>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
17817>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17817>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
17818>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
17818>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure causes the scanning of this object's items' fields,
17818>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   and the production of a set of database agents who should be 'watched'.
17818>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure depends completely upon Find_Servers_To_Watch, below.
17818>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
17818>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Scan_Servers
17820>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send find_servers_to_watch False
17821>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure scans the fields of this object's items to determine
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   what other database agents (data_sets) other than this object's Server
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   should be 'watched' (for data changes).
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure is invoked once per object, the first time the object
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   is activated.  If the data_file, data_field, and/or main_file of this
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   object are changed (don't change them while this object is active!),
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   set Private.Servers_Scanned to FALSE to force this object to scan
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   again (when it is next activated).
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // 17.0: The logic has been retooled to add more watched servers to the DDOs. This is done so
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // DD operations will send Refresh to these additional watched-servers. There are two changes:
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // 1. Containers are now made watched servers for the Server and all parent servers
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // 2. Non-file.field DEOs (e.g., expressions) are made watched servers for the server (which it
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //    already did and for all parent servers. Without this, parent entry_item expressions were not
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //    getting updated
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Here is how watched-servers works.
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Each DEO attaches and detaches from its Server by sending Add_User_interface and Remove_User_interface
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // to the server DD. Once attached, the DD knows about this DEO and sends messages to it as needed (Refresh,
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Entry_Update, etc.). In addition, a DEO may need to attach a parent DDO so that changes in that parent DD
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // results in those messages being sent. This is needed if the binding table in entry_item refers to a parent
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // table. So we need to send Add_User_interface and Remove_User_interface to that parent server as well. If a DEO
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // has multiple, there could be multiple parent servers. As of 17.0, we are also attaching to parent servers if
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // we are unsure about how the DEO is being used. If an expression is used, it might need to be updated when
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // a parent (or any ancestor) changes. Each DEO keeps track of servers that it attaches to and this is referred
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // to as the watched_server list. This list is maintained so the DEO knows which DDOs to attach and detach to.
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
17822>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure find_servers_to_watch Integer tableFlag
17824>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer i file# obj# maxitems count p srvr# self# srvrfile
17824>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        String fileStr fStr
17824>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bContainer bDoAll
17824>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
17824>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Client_Area_State to bContainer
17825>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set private.Servers_Scanned to True
17826>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
17826>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to srvr#
17827>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
17827>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (srvr#=0) Begin
17829>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return
17830>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
17830>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17830>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
17830>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send delete_watched_servers  //empty Watched_Servers broadcaster first
17831>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
17831>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get main_file of srvr# to srvrfile  // data-set's main-file
17832>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
17832>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If bContainer Begin
17834>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // containers should get added to all parent DDOs
17834>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send WatchAllParentServers srvr#
17835>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return
17836>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
17836>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17836>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
17836>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (tableFlag <> 0) ;            Get Prototype_Object to self# // tables
17839>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Else ;            Move Self to self# // forms and text windows
17841>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
17841>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get item_count of self# to maxitems
17842>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Decrement maxitems
17843>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
17843>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // if no items do nothing
17843>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // if one item do quick check
17843>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // if multiple items do it the hard way
17843>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
17843>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (maxitems<0) Begin
17845>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // if no items, which is unusual, we don't know what this DEO is so we will treat it like a container
17845>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // and add it as a watched server for all DDOs
17845>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send WatchAllParentServers srvr#
17846>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return  // no items
17847>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
17847>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17847>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
17847>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (maxitems=0) Begin // only 1 item - skip most of the nonsense
17849>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get data_file of self# 0 to file#
17850>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // we need watched server if file exists, it is not the main file
17850>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // and is not an updating file (as opposed to updating data-set).
17850>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (file#>0 and file#<>srvrfile) Begin
17852>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Get which_data_set of srvr# file# to obj#
17853>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If (obj# <> 0 and obj# <> srvr#) Begin
17855>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Send add_Watched_server obj#
17856>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Send add_ChangedStateWatched_Servers obj#
17857>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                End
17857>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17857>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
17857>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17857>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Else If (file#=0) Begin
17860>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                // if no file (e.g., expression) we don't know when it changes so we tell all servers
17860>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                // that this is a watcher
17860>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send WatchAllParentServers srvr#
17861>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
17861>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17861>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If File# ;                Send Copy_Item_Options Srvr# file# (Data_Field(Self#,0)) Self# 0
17864>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
17864>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17864>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin  // multiple items - do what you must
17865>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Move -1 to count
17866>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Move "," to fileStr
17867>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If tableFlag Begin
17869>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Get main_file to file#
17870>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If (file# <> srvrfile) Begin    // only do this if mainfile is not the srvr file
17872>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Append fileStr file# ","   //insert mainfile to be sure it's watched
17874>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Increment count
17875>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                End
17875>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17875>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
17875>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17875>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            For i from 0 to maxitems
17881>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17881>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Get data_file of self# i to file#
17882>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If (file#=0) Begin
17884>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    // as soon as we don't know what the item is used for we will have
17884>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    // to attach to all parent DDOs.
17884>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Move True to bDoAll
17885>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                End
17885>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17885>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If (file# > 0 and file#<>srvrfile and ;                    not(fileStr contains (","+String(file#)+",")) ) Begin
17887>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Move (fileStr+String(file#) + ",") to fileStr
17888>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Increment count
17889>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                End
17889>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17889>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If File# ;                    Send Copy_Item_Options Srvr# file# (Data_Field(Self#,i)) Self# i
17892>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Loop
17893>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17893>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            
17893>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // if an item's binding table is unknown, we watch all parent DDOs.
17893>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If bDoAll Begin
17895>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send WatchAllParentServers srvr#
17896>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
17896>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17896>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Else Begin
17897>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If (count >= 0) Begin // any watched items?
17899>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Move (Right(fileStr, length(fileStr) - 1))  to fileStr  //remove leading comma
17900>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    For i from 0 to count
17906>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17906>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                        Move (Pos( "," ,fileStr)) to p
17907>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                        If (p > 1) Begin
17909>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                            Move (Left( fileStr , p-1)) to fStr
17910>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                            Move (Right( fileStr, length(fileStr) - p)) to fileStr
17911>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                            Move fStr to file#
17912>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                            Get which_data_set of srvr# file# to obj#
17913>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                            If (obj# <> 0 and obj# <> srvr#) Begin
17915>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                                Send add_Watched_server obj#
17916>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                                Send add_ChangedStateWatched_Servers obj#
17917>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                            End
17917>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17917>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                        End
17917>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17917>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Loop
17918>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17918>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                End
17918>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17918>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
17918>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17918>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
17918>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17918>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
17919>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
17919>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This does nothing. Other sub-classes (or later mixins) should add
17919>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // logic to this.
17919>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Copy_Item_Options Integer iDSO Integer iFile Integer iField ;            Integer iDEO Integer iItem
17921>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
17922>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
17922>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This does little. Other sub-classes (or later mixins) should add
17922>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // logic to this.
17922>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Define_Extended_DEO_Mixin
17924>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
17925>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
17925>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
17925>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // created for Nesting support
17925>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Mark_As_Component
17927>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer ser#
17927>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Component_State to True
17928>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Set Has_Components_State to True
17930>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get private.Server to ser#
17931>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (ser# = 0) Begin
17933>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Delegate Get Locate_Server to ser#
17935>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (ser# <> 0) ;                Set private.Server to ser#
17938>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
17938>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17938>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
17939>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
17939>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This only gets called when the developer is killing this object. During application
17939>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // shut-down, only destroy_object is called. This augmentation destroys the watched broadcaster
17939>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // (which is sitting on the desktop). During program shut down we don't care if this is called
17939>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // because it is getting destroyed anyway. We are making the assumption that a developer controlled
17939>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // destroy will always be called with the watcher still existing.
17939>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
17939>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Destroy
17941>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoWatched
17941>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Changed_State to False //   is this really needed anymore???
17942>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // if non 0, The watched server, must still exist.
17942>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Watched_Servers to hoWatched
17943>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatched Begin
17945>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Broadcast_State of hoWatched to False
17946>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Destroy of hoWatched     // destroy the bcaster
17947>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
17947>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17947>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // if non 0, The bound watched server, must still exist.
17947>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get ChangedStateWatched_Servers to hoWatched
17948>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatched Begin
17950>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Broadcast_State of hoWatched to False
17951>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Destroy of hoWatched     // destroy the bcaster
17952>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
17952>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
17952>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Forward Send Destroy
17954>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
17955>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
17955>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
17955>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Should_Save Returns Integer
17957>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer Obj# Chngd
17957>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to Obj#
17958>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Changed_state to Chngd
17959>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return ( Chngd or (obj# <> 0 and Should_Save(obj#)) )
17960>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
17961>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
17961>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Added server scan logic here instead of add_focus.
17961>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Attach_Deo_To_Server
17963>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer obj# isclient srvscn wsrvr
17963>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to obj#
17964>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get client_area_state to isclient
17965>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (obj# <> 0) ;            Send add_user_interface to obj# Self
17968>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get private.Servers_Scanned to srvscn
17969>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (srvscn = 0) ;            Send scan_servers
17972>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Watched_Servers to wsrvr
17973>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If wsrvr Send add_user_interface ;            to wsrvr Self True // TRUE for watchers
17976>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (obj# <> 0 and isclient = 0) ;            Send update_dependent_items
17979>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
17980>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
17980>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Removed server scan logic and moved it to attach-deo_to_server
17980>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Add_Focus Handle hoParent Returns Integer
17982>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer srvscn retval msg
17982>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        //
17982>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // standard DEO behavior
17982>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        //
17982>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Forward Get msg_Add_Focus hoParent to retval
17984>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If retval ;            Procedure_Return retval
17987>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
17987>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (client_area_State(Self) = 0) ; //clients already broadcast            Broadcast NO_STOP Send add_focus Self
17992>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        //
17992>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // server augmentation
17992>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        //
17992>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (focus_mode(Self) <> NO_ACTIVATE and Active_State(Self)) ;            Send attach_DEO_to_server
17995>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
17995>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // last thing to do is send custom message. With list deos
17995>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // msg is probably initialize_list. With non-list deos it
17995>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // is probably nothing
17995>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get add_focus_msg to msg
17996>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If msg ;            Send msg
17999>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18000>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18000>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Connect DEO to Server if Demanded (DoAllfg=t) or ;
18000>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // allowed  (static_server_State=t). Broadcast if children exist
18000>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Connect_DEOs_to_Servers Integer DoAllFg
18002>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (DoAllfg or Static_Server_State(Self)) ;            Send Attach_Deo_to_Server
18005>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (Has_Components_State(Self)) ;            Broadcast Send Connect_DEOs_to_Servers DoAllfg
18009>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18010>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18010>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Disconnect DEOs from Servers according to rules. Broadcast
18010>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // to child components.
18010>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
18010>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Pass: DoAllMode
18010>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //    DETACH_NEVER        Never
18010>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //    DETACH_IF_NO_CHANGE Do if changed_state=F
18010>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //    DETACH_ALWAYS       Do it no matter what
18010>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //    DETACH_IF_ALLOWED   Do if changed_state=F and auto_attach
18010>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //                        (I don't think this will be needed!)
18010>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
18010>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Disconnect_DEOs_from_Servers Integer DoAllMode
18012>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (DoAllMode <> DETACH_NEVER) Begin
18014>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If ( DoAllMode=DETACH_ALWAYS or ; // do all no matter what                ( (Changed_state(Self)=0) and ;                ( (DoAllMode=DETACH_IF_NO_CHANGE) or  ;                (Static_Server_State(Self)) ) ) ) ;                Send Remove_deo_from_server
18017>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (Has_Components_State(Self)) ;                Broadcast Send Disconnect_DEOs_from_Servers DoAllMode
18021>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18021>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18021>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18022>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18022>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Changed to not remove from server if static.
18022>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Remove_Object
18024>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Forward Send remove_object
18026>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // remove if not static and no changes
18026>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If ( Static_Server_State(Self)=0 and ;            Changed_State(Self)=0 ) ;  // only detach if unchanged!            Send remove_DEO_from_server
18029>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18030>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18030>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18030>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // (JJT) Changed so that this respects Change_disabled_state. I don't
18030>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //       like this here but its the best I can think of. Therefore, all
18030>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //       objects using server.pkg must understand Change_disabled_state.
18030>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
18030>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // (JJT) Checks deferred_state and if set do not change the
18030>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // changed state of the server object. This had been in datalist and is
18030>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // required to make deferred_state work right. Deferred_state was created
18030>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // to make selection-lists work correctly and as far as I am concerned it
18030>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // should be the only supported use of this. Therefore, I would not *ever*
18030>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // expect deferred_state to be set true in tables, entry_forms, or text_
18030>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // windows. Since deferred-state is known to this mixin the change
18030>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // belongs here - but I expect it to only ever change behaviors in
18030>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // selection-lists.
18030>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18030>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18030>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Changed to not remove from server if static.
18030>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Changed_State Integer newVal
18032>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer srvr# wsrvr
18032>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If not (Change_Disabled_State(Self)) Begin
18034>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Forward Set Changed_State to newVal
18036>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get server to srvr#
18037>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            
18037>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // if deferred keep the server out of it.
18037>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If not (deferred_State(Self)) Begin
18039>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If (newVal and srvr#) Begin
18041>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Set Changed_State of srvr# to True
18042>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    // We also set changed_state of all "foreign" servers. These
18042>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    // are the ones whose Data_File is a parent File
18042>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Get ChangedStateWatched_Servers to wsrvr
18043>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    If wsrvr ;                        Set Changed_State of wSrvr to True
18046>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                End
18046>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18046>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                
18046>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                // Remove is changed-state=false, not active and not static
18046>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If ( not(newVal) and not(Active_State(Self)) and ;                    not(Static_Server_State(Self)) ) ;                    Send remove_DEO_from_Server
18049>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
18049>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18049>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18049>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18049>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18050>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18050>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // When an object is created this sets the default value for
18050>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Static_Server_state. If a parent DEO exists it will use its
18050>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // static_server_state property. An Entry_view_Client0 object sets
18050>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // this - this way view based daf programs will use the new behavior
18050>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // (although it can be disabled)  but non-daf programs will work like
18050>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // they always did.
18050>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Default_Static_Server_State Returns Integer
18052>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer rVal
18052>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // We delegate to get the actual (not default) static state
18052>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // Note: Can't check with component_state - it not defined yet
18052>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Static_Server_State to rVal
18054>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return rVal
18055>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
18056>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18056>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This adds every parent DDO for the passed DDO to the DEO's list of DDOs to watch.
18056>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // It adds the parents and then does this recursively up the DDO tree.
18056>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This means that this DEO will respond to any DD change for any server. This does not
18056>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure WatchAllParentServers Handle hoDDO
18058>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoSrvr
18058>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iServer iServers
18058>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Server_Count of hoDDO to iServers
18059>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        For iServer from 0 to (iServers-1)
18065>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18065>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server of hoDDO iServer to hoSrvr
18066>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Add_Watched_Server hoSrvr
18067>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send WatchAllParentServers hoSrvr
