18626>>>>>>>>>>>>>Register_Procedure DeleteConfirmation Handle hmCallBack
18626>>>>>>>>>>>>>Register_Procedure DataLossConfirmation Handle hmCallBack
18626>>>>>>>>>>>>>Register_Procedure SaveClearCancelConfirmation Handle hmCallBack
18626>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18626>>>>>>>>>>>>>// This provides DEO to DDO server support for Web DEOs.
18626>>>>>>>>>>>>>//
18626>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Notes:
18626>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Property Add_Focus_msg   - not supported.
18626>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Property Deferred_State  - not supported.
18626>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Property Default_static_server_state - not supported.
18626>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Property Refresh_Dirty_State         - not supported
18626>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Property Static_Server_State         - not supported.
18626>>>>>>>>>>>>>//
18626>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Function Find_Server - not supported.
18626>>>>>>>>>>>>>Class cWebBaseDEOServer is a cWebBaseUIObject
18627>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   Server is the object id of the database agent for this object.
18627>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
18627>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   Watched_Servers is a set of object ids for database agents whose state
18627>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   must also be monitored by this object (but which never receive requests
18627>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   directly from this object, unlike the Server).
18627>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
18627>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   Servers_Scanned determines if the items of this object have been
18627>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   scanned to see if this object should be connected to other database
18627>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   agents as 'just watching' (see Watched_Servers, above).
18627>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
18627>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Construct_Object
18629>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Forward Send Construct_Object
18631>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18631>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Boolean Auto_Fill_State False       // Used to tell DDO's whether first record should be found automatically after a clear.
18632>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Boolean pbAutoFillOnInit False      // Used to tell DDO's that we want autofill on initialization when DEO is attaching
18633>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18633>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer private_Server 0
18634>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Watched_Servers 0          // Handle to Broadcaster object broacasting tos server DDO's
18635>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // used to send Set Changed_State to "foreign" servers, while Watched_Servers
18635>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // is used for sending messages from the DDO to DEOs (there are more of them)
18635>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer ChangedStateWatched_Servers     0
18636>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer private_pbServersScanned 0
18637>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18637>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // added to support DEO request-delegation. This is set true if the
18637>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // server is explicitly set in this DEO (normally via a USING parameter).
18637>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Explicit_Server_State False
18638>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18638>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // Since this package's SET changed_state is using change_disabled_state
18638>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // we might as well Define it here. This gets changed by Clear_mx to support
18638>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // setting of defaults without changing the objects changed_state.
18638>>>>>>>>>>>>>        //
18638>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // This stops changed_state from getting changed. It allows item_changed_state
18638>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // to change without the object's changed_state getting changed. This Should
18638>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // be considered protected (i.e., likely to change). The new messages Entry_Defaults
18638>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // and Set Default_Value are both public and Use this. Try to use these messages
18638>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // instead of this Property.
18638>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Change_Disabled_State False
18639>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18639>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Boolean Extended_DEO_State False    // Defines DEO behavior according to Extended_DEO_State of the server DDO
18640>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18640>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Boolean Active_State False          // True when the DEO has been attached to the DDO
18641>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18641>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Handle Verify_Save_msg (RefProc(SaveConfirmation))
18642>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Handle Verify_Data_Loss_msg (RefProc(DataLossConfirmation))
18643>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Handle Verify_Delete_msg (RefProc(DeleteConfirmation))
18644>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18644>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // pbClearAfterSave: When true forces a DDO Request_Clear after performing a Request_Save. This property is reached
18644>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // via delegation from the DEO that processes the Request_Save operation. Thus this property will control the
18644>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // behavior for all DEOs belonging to this view.
18644>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Boolean pbClearAfterSave True
18645>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18645>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // Determines if the Delete callback is allowed, is set to true when the verification dialog is shown. Additional security check.
18645>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Boolean pbDeleteCallbackActive False
18648>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // Determines if the Save callback is allowed, is set to true when the verification dialog is shown. Additional security check.
18648>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Boolean pbSaveCallbackActive False
18651>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18651>>>>>>>>>>>>>        WebPublishProcedure RequestClearCallback
18652>>>>>>>>>>>>>        WebPublishProcedure RequestDeleteCallback
18653>>>>>>>>>>>>>        WebPublishProcedure RequestSaveCallBack
18654>>>>>>>>>>>>>        WebPublishProcedure RequestClearAllCallback
18655>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18656>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18656>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18656>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This procedure adds the specified object id (hoServer) to this object's
18656>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // set of database agents who are merely 'watched', and establishes a
18656>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // connection between the database agent and this object.
18656>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
18656>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Add_Watched_Server Integer hoServer
18658>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iIndex
18658>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoWatchedServers
18658>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18658>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Watched_Servers to hoWatchedServers
18659>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (hoWatchedServers = 0) Begin
18661>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Create of Desktop U_Broadcaster to hoWatchedServers // modern syntax
18662>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Watched_Servers to hoWatchedServers
18663>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18663>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18663>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18663>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Broadcast_State of hoWatchedServers to False
18664>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Find_Element of hoWatchedServers hoServer to iIndex
18665>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18665>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iIndex < 0) Begin
18667>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Add_Element to hoWatchedServers hoServer
18668>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18668>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18668>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18668>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Broadcast_State of hoWatchedServers to True
18669>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18669>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iIndex < 0 and Active_State(Self)) Begin
18671>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Add_User_Interface to hoServer Self True // TRUE for watchers
18672>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18672>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18672>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18673>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18673>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Add_ChangedStateWatched_Server Integer hoServer
18675>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iIndex
18675>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoWatchedServers
18675>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18675>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get ChangedStateWatched_Servers to hoWatchedServers
18676>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (hoWatchedServers = 0) Begin
18678>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Create of Desktop U_Broadcaster to hoWatchedServers // modern syntax
18679>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set ChangedStateWatched_Servers to hoWatchedServers
18680>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18680>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18680>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18680>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Broadcast_State of hoWatchedServers to False
18681>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Find_Element of hoWatchedServers hoServer to iIndex
18682>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18682>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iIndex < 0) Begin
18684>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Add_Element to hoWatchedServers hoServer
18685>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18685>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18685>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18685>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Broadcast_State of hoWatchedServers to True
18686>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18687>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18687>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18687>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Expects the class to understand the Active_State property. Relies on the pbDataBindable interface.
18687>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Attach_Deo_To_Server
18689>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer hoServer hoWatchedServers
18689>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bServerScan bDataBindable
18689>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18689>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoServer
18690>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get pbDataBindable to bDataBindable
18691>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18691>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (hoServer <> 0) Begin
18693>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Add_User_Interface to hoServer Self
18694>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // Extended_DEO_State is used to determine whether the object receives the data binding related
18694>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // message interface from the server DDO...
18694>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Extended_DEO_State to (Extended_DSO_State(hoServer) and bDataBindable)
18695>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18695>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18695>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18695>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get private_pbServersScanned to bServerScan
18696>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (not(bServerScan)) Begin
18698>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Scan_Servers
18699>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18699>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18699>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18699>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Watched_Servers to hoWatchedServers
18700>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatchedServers Begin
18702>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Add_User_Interface to hoWatchedServers Self True // True for watchers
18703>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18703>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18703>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18703>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Active_State to True
18704>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18705>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18705>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18705>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Changed so that this respects Change_disabled_state. I don't
18705>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // like this here but its the best I can think of. Therefore, all
18705>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // objects using server.pkg must understand Change_disabled_state.
18705>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
18705>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Changed to not remove from server if static.
18705>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Changed_State Integer newVal
18707>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer hoServer hoWatchedServers
18707>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18707>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If not (Change_Disabled_State(Self)) Begin
18709>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get server to hoServer
18710>>>>>>>>>>>>>            
18710>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (newVal and hoServer) Begin
18712>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Set Changed_State of hoServer to True
18713>>>>>>>>>>>>>                // We also set changed_state of all "foreign" servers. These
18713>>>>>>>>>>>>>                // are the ones whose Data_File is a parent File
18713>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Get ChangedStateWatched_Servers to hoWatchedServers
18714>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If hoWatchedServers ;                    Set Changed_State of hoWatchedServers to True
18717>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
18717>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18717>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18717>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18717>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18718>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18718>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // returns the table's status for the refresh event. A table can either be
18718>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // cleared, found or not touched by the operation. This can only be called while
18718>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // within Refresh. This was created to hide the private is_file_included command
18718>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function DDRefreshTableStatus Integer iTable Returns Integer
18720>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bIncluded
18720>>>>>>>>>>>>>        is_file_included iTable 1 to bIncluded // see if main file is in find done array
18722>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If bIncluded Begin
18724>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Function_Return ddrtsFound
18725>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18725>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18725>>>>>>>>>>>>>        is_file_included iTable 0 to bIncluded // see if main file is in clear done array
18727>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If bIncluded Begin
18729>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Function_Return ddrtsCleared
18730>>>>>>>>>>>>>            
18730>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18730>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18730>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return ddrtsNone
18731>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
18732>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18732>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18732>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18732>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure empties the Watched_Servers broadcaster, after
18732>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   detaching this object from all of the broadcaster's elements.
18732>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure is invoked by Find_Servers_to_Watch, in preparation
18732>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   for a scan.
18732>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Delete_Watched_Servers
18734>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer hoWatchedServers
18734>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18734>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Watched_Servers to hoWatchedServers
18735>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatchedServers Begin
18737>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Remove_User_Interface to hoWatchedServers Self True // detach from all, TRUE for watchers
18738>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of hoWatchedServers to False
18739>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Delete_Data to hoWatchedServers                     // empty it
18740>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of hoWatchedServers to True
18741>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18741>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18741>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18741>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get ChangedStateWatched_Servers to hoWatchedServers
18742>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatchedServers Begin
18744>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of hoWatchedServers to False
18745>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Delete_Data to hoWatchedServers                     // empty it
18746>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of hoWatchedServers to True
18747>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18747>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18747>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18748>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18748>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Required DD/DEO interface. Indicates if this DEO is a data bindable control or a container.
18748>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // For cWebControls, this is just another way of querying pbDataBindable, used by DD's
18748>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function DEO_Control_Object Returns Boolean
18750>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bDataBindable
18750>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get pbDataBindable to bDataBindable
18751>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return bDataBindable
18752>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
18753>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18753>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Required DD/DEO interface. Indicates that this DEO understands the DEO Request_Find protocol
18753>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function DEO_Find_Object Returns Boolean
18755>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return False
18756>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
18757>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18757>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Used to determine if the object understands the DEO interface.
18757>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Probably not used in Ajax WebApps.
18757>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function DEO_Object Returns Boolean
18759>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return True
18760>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
18761>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18761>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This only gets called when the developer is killing this object. During application
18761>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // shut-down, only destroy_object is called. This augmentation destroys the watched broadcaster
18761>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // (which is sitting on the desktop). During program shut down we don't care if this is called
18761>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // because it is getting destroyed anyway. We are making the assumption that a developer controlled
18761>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // destroy will always be called with the watcher still existing.
18761>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Destroy
18763>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoWatched
18763>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Changed_State to False //   is this really needed anymore???
18764>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // if non 0, The watched server, must still exist.
18764>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Watched_Servers to hoWatched
18765>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatched Begin
18767>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Broadcast_State of hoWatched to False
18768>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Destroy of hoWatched     // destroy the broadcaster
18769>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18769>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18769>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // if non 0, The bound watched server, must still exist.
18769>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get ChangedStateWatched_Servers to hoWatched
18770>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatched Begin
18772>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Broadcast_State of hoWatched to False
18773>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Destroy of hoWatched     // destroy the broadcaster
18774>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18774>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18774>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Forward Send Destroy
18776>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18777>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18777>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18777>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Required DD/DEO interface
18777>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // sent by DD before a find and save. We only care about DD finds which
18777>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // means DoAll is 1
18777>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Entry_Update Integer iFile Integer iDoAll
18779>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // STUB: Not used with Ajax WebApp
18779>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure scans the fields of this object's items to determine
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   what other database agents (data_sets) other than this object's Server
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   should be 'watched' (for data changes).
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   iTableFlag is a boolean determining whether this object relies on a
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   prototype row (TRUE) or an item list (FALSE).
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   [JVH] VDF 17.0 - Ignored in this class.
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This object must understand pbDataBindable, and have a private
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   boolean property named Private_pbServersScanned to note the event.
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Notes
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure is invoked once per object, the first time the object
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   is activated.  If the data_file, data_field, and/or main_file of this
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   object are changed (don't change them while this object is active!),
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   set Private_pbServersScanned to FALSE to force this object to scan
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   again (when it is next activated).
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // 17.0: The logic has been retooled to add more watched servers to the DDOs. This is done so
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // DD operations will send Refresh to these additional watched-servers. There are two changes:
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // 1. Containers are now made watched servers for the Server and all parent servers
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // 2. Non-file.field DEOs (e.g., expressions) are made watched servers for the server (which it
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //    already did and for all parent servers. Without this, parent entry_item expressions were not
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //    getting updated
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Here is how watched-servers works.
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Each DEO attaches and detaches from its Server by sending Add_User_interface and Remove_User_interface
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // to the server DD. Once attached, the DD knows about this DEO and sends messages to it as needed (Refresh,
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Entry_Update, etc.). In addition, a DEO may need to attach a parent DDO so that changes in that parent DD
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // results in those messages being sent. This is needed if the binding table in entry_item refers to a parent
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // table. So we need to send Add_User_interface and Remove_User_interface to that parent server as well. If a DEO
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // has multiple, there could be multiple parent servers. As of 17.0, we are also attaching to parent servers if
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // we are unsure about how the DEO is being used. If an expression is used, it might need to be updated when
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // a parent (or any ancestor) changes. Each DEO keeps track of servers that it attaches to and this is referred
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // to as the watched_server list. This list is maintained so the DEO knows which DDOs to attach and detach to.
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // [JVH] VDF 17.1 cWebAppDEOServer_mixin Notes:
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // - Modified to support only 1 item per control. Get Item_Count interface not supported.
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // - Modified to not support the Prototype_Object interface (old windows Table class).
18780>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Find_Servers_To_Watch Integer iTableFlag
18782>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFileNum iServerFile
18782>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoServer hoDataSet
18782>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bDataBindable
18782>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18782>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get pbDataBindable to bDataBindable
18783>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Private_pbServersScanned to True
18784>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoServer
18785>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18785>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (hoServer = 0) Begin
18787>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return
18788>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18788>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18788>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18788>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Delete_Watched_Servers  // empty Watched_Servers broadcaster first
18789>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Main_File of hoServer to iServerFile  // data-set's main-file
18790>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18790>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (not(bDataBindable)) Begin
18792>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // containers should get added to all parent DDOs
18792>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send WatchAllParentServers hoServer
18793>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return
18794>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18794>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18794>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18794>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_File to iFileNum
18795>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // we need watched server if file exists, it is not the main file
18795>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // and is not an updating file (as opposed to updating data-set).
18795>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iFileNum > 0 and iFileNum <> iServerFile) Begin
18797>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Which_Data_Set of hoServer iFileNum to hoDataSet
18798>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (hoDataSet <> 0 and hoDataSet <> hoServer) Begin
18800>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send Add_Watched_Server hoDataSet
18801>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send Add_ChangedStateWatched_Server hoDataSet
18802>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
18802>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18802>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18802>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18802>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Else If (iFileNum = 0) Begin
18805>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // if no file (e.g., expression) we don't know when it changes so we tell all servers
18805>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // that this is a watcher
18805>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send WatchAllParentServers hoServer
18806>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18806>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18806>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18807>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18807>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This function returns the object id of the database agent of this object,
18807>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // or 0.
18807>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Locate_Server Returns Integer
18809>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoServer
18809>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoServer
18810>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return hoServer
18811>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
18812>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18812>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Refresh Integer eMode
18814>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18815>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18815>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure discontinues the connection between this object and its
18815>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   database agent(s) (Server and Watched_Servers).
18815>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Remove_DEO_From_Server
18817>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer hoServer hoWatchedServers
18817>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18817>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoServer
18818>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18818>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (hoServer <> 0) Begin
18820>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Remove_User_Interface to hoServer Self
18821>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18821>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18821>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18821>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // Only send if watched-server exists
18821>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Watched_Servers to hoWatchedServers
18822>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18822>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatchedServers Begin
18824>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Remove_User_Interface to hoWatchedServers Self True // TRUE for watchers
18825>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18825>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18825>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18825>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // when removed the deo is no longer up to date.
18825>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Refresh_Dirty_State to True
18826>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18827>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18827>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18827>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure removes the specified object id (hoServer) from this object's
18827>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   set of database agents who are merely 'watched', and destroys the
18827>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   connection between the database agent and this object.
18827>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Remove_Watched_Server Integer hoServer
18829>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iIndex
18829>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoWatchedServers
18829>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18829>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Watched_Servers to hoWatchedServers
18830>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // Only if w server exists
18830>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatchedServers Begin
18832>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of hoWatchedServers to False
18833>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get find_element of hoWatchedServers hoServer to iIndex
18834>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (iIndex >= 0) Begin
18836>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send remove_element to hoWatchedServers hoServer
18837>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
18837>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18837>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of hoWatchedServers to True
18838>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (iIndex >= 0 and Active_State(Self)) Begin
18840>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send Remove_User_Interface to hoServer Self True // TRUE for watchers
18841>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
18841>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18841>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18841>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18841>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18842>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18842>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18842>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This function returns the object id of the database agent of this object, or 0.
18842>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // If this object's Server is 0, this object's parent's Server is returned, if any.
18842>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This function is used to allow nested data-entry objects to use the
18842>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // database agent defined by their parent object.
18842>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Server Returns Integer
18844>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer hoServer
18844>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get private_Server to hoServer
18845>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (hoServer = 0) Begin
18847>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Function_Return (Locate_Server(parent(Self)))
18848>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18848>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18848>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return hoServer
18849>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
18850>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18850>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18850>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This procedure sets the value of the Server property of this object,
18850>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // notifying child-objects of the change, and destroying and creating
18850>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // connections with database agents, as required.
18850>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // If the Server of this object is changed while this object is inactive,
18850>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // no notification of child-objects is required or performed.
18850>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Server Integer newVal
18852>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer oldVal
18852>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18852>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Explicit_Server_State to (newVal <> 0)
18853>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to oldVal
18854>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18854>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (newVal <> 0) Begin
18856>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set private_Server to (object_id(newVal))
18857>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18857>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18857>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
18858>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set private_Server to newVal
18859>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18859>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18859>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18859>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (Active_State(Self)) Begin
18861>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Broadcast Send server_changed oldVal newVal
18863>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (oldVal <> 0) Begin
18865>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send Remove_DEO_From_Server  // detach from current server
18866>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
18866>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18866>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (newval <> 0) Begin
18868>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send Attach_Deo_To_Server    // attach to new server
18869>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
18869>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18869>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18869>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18869>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18870>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18870>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18870>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure servers as notification of a change in the connection
18870>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   of this object's parent to its database agent.  If this object uses
18870>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   its parent's database agent by default (see the Server and Find_Server
18870>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   functions, above), it must disconnect from the old agent and connect
18870>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   with the new agent.
18870>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Server_Changed Integer oldVal Integer newVal
18872>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer oldSrvr
18872>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
18872>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get private_Server to oldSrvr
18873>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (oldSrvr = 0) Begin  //assumes Server(self) = oldVal by deleg
18875>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (oldVal <> 0) ;                Send remove_user_interface to oldVal Self
18878>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (newVal <> 0) ;                Send add_user_interface to newVal Self
18881>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18881>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18881>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
18882>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18882>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
18882>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // return the DEO that sets the server
18882>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function ServerDEO Returns Handle
18884>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoServer hoServerDeo
18884>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bExplicitServer
18884>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoServer
18885>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (hoServer) Begin
18887>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Explicit_Server_State to bExplicitServer
18888>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (bExplicitServer) Begin
18890>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Move Self to hoServerDeo
18891>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
18891>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18891>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Else Begin
18892>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Delegate Get ServerDEO to hoServerDeo
18894>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
18894>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18894>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
18894>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
18894>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return hoServerDeo
18895>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
18896>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
