19313>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19313>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // 3/22/2002: Added find_first and Find_last. Previously this
19313>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // was accomplished by sending beginning_of_data and end_of_data. The
19313>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // problem with that message is that it had multiple meaning. In a edit
19313>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // or grid, it means go to top/bottom of file. In forms, it means first
19313>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // last record. Since we can not change this without breaking existing
19313>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // programs we will create a message that *always* does a find first/last
19313>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // record. This can be used in tool bars (or anywhere) to consistently provide
19313>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // the same behavior.
19313>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19313>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Find_First
19315>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Request_Find FIRST_RECORD False // param is false because entry-update is not needed
19316>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19317>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19317>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Find_Last
19319>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Request_Find LAST_RECORD False
19320>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19321>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19321>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure SuperFind
19323>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Request_SuperFind GE
19324>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19325>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19325>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure SuperFind_Next
19327>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Request_SuperFind GT
19328>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19329>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19329>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure SuperFind_Previous
19331>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Request_SuperFind LT
19332>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
