21736>>>>>>>>>
21736>>>>>>>>>    // Sent when a refind record fails during one of the refind records operation 
21736>>>>>>>>>    // By default it does nothing, but it can raise an error and allows for careful customization
21736>>>>>>>>>    //
21736>>>>>>>>>    // hoDDO is the DDO that had the refind failure.
21736>>>>>>>>>    // This failed because RowId record cannot be refound or the RowId record is not 
21736>>>>>>>>>    // constraint valid.
21736>>>>>>>>>    //
21736>>>>>>>>>    // eOperation tells you what operation caused this:
21736>>>>>>>>>    // 0 - reoUndefined: should not get called with this
21736>>>>>>>>>    // 1 - reoSyncDDOs: During a request resync 
21736>>>>>>>>>    // 2 - reoNavigateForward: After resync during a NavigateForward
21736>>>>>>>>>    // 3 - reoNavigateBack: After resync during a NavigateBack 
21736>>>>>>>>>    // 4 - reoRefreshRecord: during RefreshRecord.
21736>>>>>>>>>    //
21736>>>>>>>>>    // eReason tells you the type of record find failure. 
21736>>>>>>>>>    // These only apply to NavigateForward|Back
21736>>>>>>>>>    // 0 - retUndefined
21736>>>>>>>>>    // 1 - retCannotRereadMain: Failed rereading the main file
21736>>>>>>>>>    // 2 - retCannotRereadConstrainingParent: Failed rereading a constraining parent
21736>>>>>>>>>    // 
21736>>>>>>>>>    // If you place a breakpoint here, you've got a place where all refind errors
21736>>>>>>>>>    // are redirected - very useful for debugging.
21736>>>>>>>>>
21736>>>>>>>>>    Procedure OnRefindRecordError Handle hoDD Integer eOperation Integer eReason
21738>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bShowAllRefindErrors
21738>>>>>>>>>        
21738>>>>>>>>>        // pbShowAllRefindErrors is cWebApp property, set it true when debugging to see all
21738>>>>>>>>>        // errors. This assumes that a refind error during debugging is probably a programming bug.
21738>>>>>>>>>        
21738>>>>>>>>>        Get pbShowAllRefindErrors to bShowAllRefindErrors
21739>>>>>>>>>        If bShowAllRefindErrors Begin
21741>>>>>>>>>             Send CannotRefindRecordUnhandledError hoDD
21742>>>>>>>>>        End
21742>>>>>>>>>>
21742>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
21743>>>>>>>>>
21743>>>>>>>>>    // Sent when RefreshRecord fails. 
21743>>>>>>>>>    // By default call standard OnRefindRecordError. This allows for customization
21743>>>>>>>>>    Procedure OnRefreshRecordError Handle hoDD
21745>>>>>>>>>        Send OnRefindRecordError hoDD reoRefreshRecord retUndefined
21746>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
