26560>>>>>>>>>
26560>>>>>>>>>
26560>>>>>>>>>    // Send this message to fire an action on the client telling it to refresh the grid.
26560>>>>>>>>>    Procedure GridRefresh
26562>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bFirst bLast
26562>>>>>>>>>        tWebListData listData
26562>>>>>>>>>        tWebListData listData
26562>>>>>>>>>        String[] asParams
26563>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoJsonData
26563>>>>>>>>>                
26563>>>>>>>>>        //  We cancel previous gridRefresh client actions that might be queued before
26563>>>>>>>>>        Send CancelClientAction "gridRefresh"
26564>>>>>>>>>        
26564>>>>>>>>>        // Forward call to the load data
26564>>>>>>>>>        Get LoadData "page" "" (&bFirst) (&bLast) to listData
26565>>>>>>>>>        WebSet pbUnOrdered to False
26566>>>>>>>>>        
26566>>>>>>>>>        //  Convert data to JSON
26566>>>>>>>>>        Get Create (RefClass(cJsonObject)) to hoJsonData
26567>>>>>>>>>        Send DataTypeToJson of hoJsonData listData
26568>>>>>>>>>
26568>>>>>>>>>        //  Call client action with new data page
26568>>>>>>>>>        Move bFirst         to asParams[0]
26569>>>>>>>>>        Move bLast          to asParams[1]
26570>>>>>>>>>        Send ClientActionEx "gridRefresh" asParams hoJsonData
26571>>>>>>>>>        
26571>>>>>>>>>        Send Destroy of hoJsonData
26572>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
26573>>>>>>>>>
26573>>>>>>>>>    
26573>>>>>>>>>    // Does a empty grid refresh
26573>>>>>>>>>    Procedure EmptyGridRefresh
26575>>>>>>>>>        String[] asParams
26576>>>>>>>>>        tWebListData listData
26576>>>>>>>>>        tWebListData listData
26576>>>>>>>>>        
26576>>>>>>>>>        //  We cancel previous gridRefresh client actions that might be queued before
26576>>>>>>>>>        Send CancelClientAction "gridRefresh"
26577>>>>>>>>>        
26577>>>>>>>>>        //  Call client action with empty data set
26577>>>>>>>>>        Move True to asParams[0]
26578>>>>>>>>>        Move True to asParams[1]
26579>>>>>>>>>        Send ClientAction "gridRefresh" asParams listData
26580>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
26581>>>>>>>>>    
26581>>>>>>>>>    
26581>>>>>>>>>    // This message is sent by the client to load a page of data. Usually caused by the user 
26581>>>>>>>>>    // scrolling to the end of the virtual list.
26581>>>>>>>>>    Procedure LoadDataPage String sType String sStartRowID
26583>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bFirst bLast
26583>>>>>>>>>        tWebListData listData
26583>>>>>>>>>        tWebListData listData
26583>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoJsonData
26583>>>>>>>>>        String[] asParams
26584>>>>>>>>>        
26584>>>>>>>>>        //  Forward call to the load data
26584>>>>>>>>>        Get LoadData sType sStartRowID (&bFirst) (&bLast) to listData
26585>>>>>>>>>        
26585>>>>>>>>>        //  Convert data to JSON
26585>>>>>>>>>        Get Create (RefClass(cJsonObject)) to hoJsonData
26586>>>>>>>>>        Send DataTypeToJson of hoJsonData listData
26587>>>>>>>>>        
26587>>>>>>>>>        //  Call client action with new data page
26587>>>>>>>>>        Move sType          to asParams[0]
26588>>>>>>>>>        Move sStartRowId    to asParams[1]
26589>>>>>>>>>        Move bFirst         to asParams[2]
26590>>>>>>>>>        Move bLast          to asParams[3]
26591>>>>>>>>>        Send ClientActionEx "handleDataPage" asParams hoJsonData
26592>>>>>>>>>        
26592>>>>>>>>>        Send Destroy of hoJsonData
26593>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
26594>>>>>>>>>    
26594>>>>>>>>>    // OnManualLoadData is False - DDO LoadData
26594>>>>>>>>>    // Returns a set of data to be passed back to the client side grid.
26594>>>>>>>>>    // sType - is the type of data to be loaded. Options are: 
26594>>>>>>>>>    //         "page": returns a set of records around (above and below) the current row
26594>>>>>>>>>    //         "first": loads the first page of data
26594>>>>>>>>>    //         "last": loads the last page of data
26594>>>>>>>>>    //         "next": loads the next page of data relative to the passed sStartRowID
26594>>>>>>>>>    //         "prev": loads the previous page of data relative to the passed sStartRowID
26594>>>>>>>>>    //         Note that these values are case sensitive.
26594>>>>>>>>>    // sStartRowID - Is the server table's RowID to begin from when loading "next" or "prev" pages.
26594>>>>>>>>>    // bFirst - [out] True if the returned data is the first page in the total data set.
26594>>>>>>>>>    // bLast - [out] true if the returned data is the last page in the total data set.
26594>>>>>>>>>    //
26594>>>>>>>>>    // OnManualLoadData is True - Manual Load Data
26594>>>>>>>>>    // Populates list via OnManualLoadData and sets bFirst & bLast to True
26594>>>>>>>>>    //
26594>>>>>>>>>    // Returns - the requested page of data.
26594>>>>>>>>>    Function LoadData String sType String sStartRowID Boolean ByRef bFirst Boolean ByRef bLast Returns tWebListData
26596>>>>>>>>>        tWebListData listData
26596>>>>>>>>>        tWebListData listData
26596>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDD
26596>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMainFile iPageSize iHalfPageSize iOrdering
26596>>>>>>>>>        Integer iRow iCol icColumn iFile iField iLimit
26596>>>>>>>>>        RowID riRowID
26596>>>>>>>>>        String sValue sRowID
26596>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bUsePageSize bReverseOrdering bDataAware bLastFound bScrollable
26596>>>>>>>>>        Integer eDBGridType
26596>>>>>>>>>        Variant vFilterState
26596>>>>>>>>>
26596>>>>>>>>>        // Test if OnManualLoadData has been agumented. If this event returns True then we
26596>>>>>>>>>        // will use that to populate the grid and the DDO (data-aware) grid loading will be
26596>>>>>>>>>        // skipped.  
26596>>>>>>>>>        Get pbDataAware to bDataAware
26597>>>>>>>>>        Get peDbGridType to eDBGridType
26598>>>>>>>>>        Get pbScroll to bScrollable
26599>>>>>>>>>        
26599>>>>>>>>>        // Data is loaded manually if the data is not-data aware or if
26599>>>>>>>>>        // it is data aware and manual loaded.
26599>>>>>>>>>        If (not(bDataAware) or (eDBGridType=gtManual)) Begin      
26601>>>>>>>>>            WebGet psCurrentRowId to sRowID
26602>>>>>>>>>                
26602>>>>>>>>>            Send OnManualLoadData (&listData.aRows) (&sRowID) (&listData.aGroups) (&listData.aGroupHeaders)
26603>>>>>>>>>        
26603>>>>>>>>>            Move True to bFirst
26604>>>>>>>>>            Move True to bLast
26605>>>>>>>>>            WebSet psCurrentRowId to sRowID
26606>>>>>>>>>            Function_Return listData 
26607>>>>>>>>>        End
26607>>>>>>>>>>
26607>>>>>>>>>        
26607>>>>>>>>>        Get ReadingServer to hoDD
26608>>>>>>>>>        Get IndexOrder to iOrdering
26609>>>>>>>>>        WebGet pbReverseOrdering to bReverseOrdering
26610>>>>>>>>>        WebGet piLimitRows to iLimit
26611>>>>>>>>>
26611>>>>>>>>>        Move False to bFirst
26612>>>>>>>>>        Move False to bLast
26613>>>>>>>>>
26613>>>>>>>>>        If (hoDD) Begin
26615>>>>>>>>>            Send ApplyFilter hoDD (&vFilterState)
26616>>>>>>>>>            Move 0 to iRow
26617>>>>>>>>>            Get piPageSize to iPageSize
26618>>>>>>>>>            Move (eDBGridType=gtAutomatic and bScrollable and (iPageSize > 0)) to bUsePageSize
26619>>>>>>>>>            Get Main_File of hoDD to iMainFile
26620>>>>>>>>>            
26620>>>>>>>>>            WebGet psCurrentRowId to sRowID    // Get the RowID of the current row
26621>>>>>>>>>            Move (DeserializeRowID(sRowID)) to riRowID
26622>>>>>>>>>            If (IsNullRowID(riRowID)) Begin
26624>>>>>>>>>                // if no row id, we don't do anything. We return an empty set of rows
26624>>>>>>>>>                // and indicate that we have all the records we can find
26624>>>>>>>>>                Move True to bFirst
26625>>>>>>>>>                Move True to bLast
26626>>>>>>>>>            End
26626>>>>>>>>>>
26626>>>>>>>>>            Else Begin
26627>>>>>>>>>                // Handle the different request "types"
26627>>>>>>>>>                
26627>>>>>>>>>                // "page" request type (usually initial request) returns records 
26627>>>>>>>>>                // above and below the current row
26627>>>>>>>>>                If (sType = "page") Begin
26629>>>>>>>>>                    
26629>>>>>>>>>                    // Find half a page reading backwards from the current row
26629>>>>>>>>>                    Send ReadByRowId of hoDD iMainFile riRowID     // Read the current row
26630>>>>>>>>>    
26630>>>>>>>>>                    Send EstablishDDFindMode LT hoDD iOrdering bReverseOrdering
26631>>>>>>>>>                    Send Locate_Next to hoDD
26632>>>>>>>>>                    Move Found to bLastFound
26633>>>>>>>>>                    Move (iPageSize / 2) to iHalfPageSize
26634>>>>>>>>>                                        
26634>>>>>>>>>                    While (bLastFound and (not(bUsePageSize) or (iRow < iHalfPageSize)) and (iLimit = 0 or iRow < iLimit))
26638>>>>>>>>>                        If (OnCheckCustomConstrains(Self)) Begin
26640>>>>>>>>>                            Get LoadGridRow to listData.aRows[iRow]
26641>>>>>>>>>                            Increment iRow
26642>>>>>>>>>                        End
26642>>>>>>>>>>
26642>>>>>>>>>                        
26642>>>>>>>>>                        Send Locate_Next to hoDD
26643>>>>>>>>>                        Move Found to bLastFound    //  Store Found value since LoadGridRow triggers user events that might change the Found indicator
26644>>>>>>>>>                    Loop
26645>>>>>>>>>>
26645>>>>>>>>>                    
26645>>>>>>>>>                    Move (not(bLastFound) or (iLimit > 0 and iRow >= iLimit)) to bFirst              // Determine 'bFirst'
26646>>>>>>>>>                    Move (ReverseArray(listData.aRows)) to listData.aRows  // Now reverse the array and add the rows below the current row
26647>>>>>>>>>    
26647>>>>>>>>>                    // load the current record
26647>>>>>>>>>                    Send ReadByRowId of hoDD iMainFile riRowID
26648>>>>>>>>>                    Move Found to bLastFound
26649>>>>>>>>>                    If (OnCheckCustomConstrains(Self)) Begin
26651>>>>>>>>>                        Get LoadGridRow to listData.aRows[iRow]
26652>>>>>>>>>                        Increment iRow
26653>>>>>>>>>                    End
26653>>>>>>>>>>
26653>>>>>>>>>    
26653>>>>>>>>>                    // Find the remaining records
26653>>>>>>>>>                    Send EstablishDDFindMode GT  hoDD iOrdering bReverseOrdering
26654>>>>>>>>>                    While ((not(bUsePageSize) or (iRow < iPageSize)) and (iLimit = 0 or iRow < iLimit))
26658>>>>>>>>>                        Send Locate_Next to hoDD
26659>>>>>>>>>                        Move Found to bLastFound
26660>>>>>>>>>                        If (not(Found)) ;                            Break
26663>>>>>>>>>                        If (OnCheckCustomConstrains(Self)) Begin
26665>>>>>>>>>                            Get LoadGridRow to listData.aRows[iRow]
26666>>>>>>>>>                            Increment iRow
26667>>>>>>>>>                        End
26667>>>>>>>>>>
26667>>>>>>>>>                    Loop
26668>>>>>>>>>>
26668>>>>>>>>>                    
26668>>>>>>>>>                    // Set the bLast flag
26668>>>>>>>>>                    Move (not(bLastFound) or (iLimit > 0 and  iRow >= iLimit)) to bLast      
26669>>>>>>>>>                End
26669>>>>>>>>>>
26669>>>>>>>>>                Else Begin
26670>>>>>>>>>                    Case Begin
26670>>>>>>>>>                        Case (sType = "first")
26672>>>>>>>>>                            //  Load the first record
26672>>>>>>>>>                            // NOTE: Request_Read when called during DEO Refresh (or any other DDO operation) from DDO will screw up the
26672>>>>>>>>>                            // DDO's ability to track the array of DDO's in the DDO structure who need to be listeners to the DDO operation!
26672>>>>>>>>>                            // Therefore make sure that this case never gets called indirectly via a DDO to DEO Refresh
26672>>>>>>>>>                            Get ReadDDFirstRecord hoDD iOrdering bReverseOrdering to riRowID
26673>>>>>>>>>                            Move True to bFirst
26674>>>>>>>>>                            Case Break
26675>>>>>>>>>                        
26675>>>>>>>>>                        Case (sType = "last")
26678>>>>>>>>>                            //  Load the last record
26678>>>>>>>>>                            // NOTE: Request_Read when called during DEO Refresh (or any other DDO operation) from DDO will screw up the
26678>>>>>>>>>                            // DDO's ability to track the array of DDO's in the DDO structure who need to be listeners to the DDO operation!
26678>>>>>>>>>                            // Therefore make sure that this case never gets called indirectly via a DDO to DEO Refresh
26678>>>>>>>>>                            Get ReadDDLastRecord hoDD iOrdering bReverseOrdering to riRowID
26679>>>>>>>>>                            Move True to bLast
26680>>>>>>>>>                            Case Break
26681>>>>>>>>>                    
26681>>>>>>>>>                        Case (sType = "next")
26684>>>>>>>>>                            //  Load the start record
26684>>>>>>>>>                            Move (DeserializeRowID(sStartRowId)) to riRowID
26685>>>>>>>>>                            Send ReadByRowId of hoDD iMainFile riRowID
26686>>>>>>>>>                            Send EstablishDDFindMode GT  hoDD iOrdering bReverseOrdering
26687>>>>>>>>>                            Send Locate_Next of hoDD
26688>>>>>>>>>                            Case Break
26689>>>>>>>>>                    
26689>>>>>>>>>                        Case (sType = "prev")
26692>>>>>>>>>                            //  Load the start record
26692>>>>>>>>>                            Move (DeserializeRowID(sStartRowId)) to riRowID
26693>>>>>>>>>                            Send ReadByRowId of hoDD iMainFile riRowID
26694>>>>>>>>>                            Send EstablishDDFindMode LT  hoDD iOrdering bReverseOrdering
26695>>>>>>>>>                            Send Locate_Next of hoDD
26696>>>>>>>>>                    Case End
26696>>>>>>>>>                    Move Found to bLastFound
26697>>>>>>>>>                    
26697>>>>>>>>>                    //  Find remaining records
26697>>>>>>>>>                    While (Found and (not(bUsePageSize) or (iRow < iPageSize)) and (iLimit = 0 or iRow < iLimit))
26701>>>>>>>>>                        If (OnCheckCustomConstrains(Self)) Begin
26703>>>>>>>>>                            Get LoadGridRow to listData.aRows[iRow]
26704>>>>>>>>>                            Increment iRow
26705>>>>>>>>>                        End
26705>>>>>>>>>>
26705>>>>>>>>>                        Send Locate_Next to hoDD
26706>>>>>>>>>                        Move Found to bLastFound
26707>>>>>>>>>                    Loop
26708>>>>>>>>>>
26708>>>>>>>>>                
26708>>>>>>>>>                    // Set the bLast and bFirst flags
26708>>>>>>>>>                    If (not(bLastFound) or (iLimit > 0 and  iRow >= iLimit)) Begin
26710>>>>>>>>>                        If (sType = "next" or sType = "first") Begin
26712>>>>>>>>>                            Move True to bLast
26713>>>>>>>>>                        End
26713>>>>>>>>>>
26713>>>>>>>>>                        Else Begin
26714>>>>>>>>>                            Move True to bFirst
26715>>>>>>>>>                        End
26715>>>>>>>>>>
26715>>>>>>>>>                    End            
26715>>>>>>>>>>
26715>>>>>>>>>                End
26715>>>>>>>>>>
26715>>>>>>>>>            End
26715>>>>>>>>>>
26715>>>>>>>>>
26715>>>>>>>>>            Send DisregardFilter vFilterState
26716>>>>>>>>>        End
26716>>>>>>>>>>
26716>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
26717>>>>>>>>>            //  Stop the list from trying to find records while there is no DD
26717>>>>>>>>>            Move True to bLast
26718>>>>>>>>>            Move True to bFirst
26719>>>>>>>>>        End
26719>>>>>>>>>>
26719>>>>>>>>>
26719>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return listData
26720>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
26721>>>>>>>>>    
26721>>>>>>>>>    
26721>>>>>>>>>    // Sent by LoadData. User hook to manually populate the grid. To use this create some loop where each
26721>>>>>>>>>    // iteration populates one row of the grid.
26721>>>>>>>>>    // aTheRows      - [out] Array of tWebRow members to be populated. This is the grid data. 
26721>>>>>>>>>    //                 The aValues member should contain one array member for each column, starting with
26721>>>>>>>>>    //                 array member 1 for column one. aValues[0] should be populated with a unique RowID.
26721>>>>>>>>>    // sCurrentRowID - [out] Set this to the unique rowID of the row you wish to become the currently 
26721>>>>>>>>>    //                 selected row after the grid data is sent to the client.
26721>>>>>>>>>    Procedure OnManualLoadData tWebRow[] ByRef aTheRows String ByRef sCurrentRowID tWebGroupConfig[] ByRef aTheGroups tWebGroupHeader[] ByRef aTheGroupHeaders
26723>>>>>>>>>        
26723>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
26724>>>>>>>>>
26724>>>>>>>>>    
26724>>>>>>>>>    // Populates a single row of data.
26724>>>>>>>>>    // This is sent by LoadData when loading data from DDO server.
26724>>>>>>>>>    // It assumes that the global record buffers contain the grid row data that we want to display
26724>>>>>>>>>    // in the returned tWebGridRow.s
26724>>>>>>>>>
26724>>>>>>>>>    Function LoadGridRow Returns tWebRow
26726>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bDataAware
26726>>>>>>>>>        RowID riRowID
26726>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile iField iCol icColumn eDataType iMainFile
26726>>>>>>>>>        String sValue
26726>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDD
26726>>>>>>>>>        Handle[] aColumns
26727>>>>>>>>>        tWebRow tRow
26727>>>>>>>>>        tWebRow tRow
26727>>>>>>>>>        
26727>>>>>>>>>        Get pbDataAware to bDataAware
26728>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoDD
26729>>>>>>>>>        
26729>>>>>>>>>        Get phoColumnObjects to aColumns
26730>>>>>>>>>        Move (SizeOfArray(aColumns)) to icColumn
26731>>>>>>>>>        Move (ResizeArray(tRow.aCells, icColumn)) to tRow.aCells
26732>>>>>>>>>        Move -1 to tRow.iGroupHeaderIndex
26733>>>>>>>>>        
26733>>>>>>>>>        If (bDataAware) Begin
26735>>>>>>>>>            Get Main_File of hoDD to iMainFile
26736>>>>>>>>>            
26736>>>>>>>>>            Move (GetRowID(iMainFile)) to riRowID
26737>>>>>>>>>            Move (SerializeRowID(riRowID)) to tRow.sRowID
26738>>>>>>>>>            
26738>>>>>>>>>            // Iterate the grid columns
26738>>>>>>>>>            For iCol from 0 to (icColumn-1)
26744>>>>>>>>>>
26744>>>>>>>>>                Send LoadGridCell of aColumns[iCol] (&tRow.aCells[iCol])
26745>>>>>>>>>            Loop
26746>>>>>>>>>>
26746>>>>>>>>>        End
26746>>>>>>>>>>
26746>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
26747>>>>>>>>>            WebGet psCurrentRowId to tRow.sRowID
26748>>>>>>>>>            
26748>>>>>>>>>            //  Determine if a value was changed
26748>>>>>>>>>            For iCol from 0 to (icColumn-1)
26754>>>>>>>>>>
26754>>>>>>>>>                Send LoadGridCell of aColumns[iCol] (&tRow.aCells[iCol])
26755>>>>>>>>>            Loop
26756>>>>>>>>>>
26756>>>>>>>>>        End
26756>>>>>>>>>>
26756>>>>>>>>>        
26756>>>>>>>>>        Send OnDefineRowCssClass (&tRow.sCssClassName)
26757>>>>>>>>>        
26757>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return tRow
26758>>>>>>>>>    End_Function 
26759>>>>>>>>>    
26759>>>>>>>>>    
26759>>>>>>>>>    // Loads the row posted from the action data into the buffer. It gets the row from a the 
26759>>>>>>>>>    // paActionData property and updates the psValue from the colums with its values. It also sets 
26759>>>>>>>>>    // the psCurrentRowId to the new row.
26759>>>>>>>>>    Procedure FillFromActionData
26761>>>>>>>>>        Handle[] aColumns
26762>>>>>>>>>        tWebRow[] aActionData
26762>>>>>>>>>        tWebRow[] aActionData
26763>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoJson
26763>>>>>>>>>        tWebRow tSelectRow
26763>>>>>>>>>        tWebRow tSelectRow
26763>>>>>>>>>        Integer iCol
26763>>>>>>>>>        String sValue
26763>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bCol
26763>>>>>>>>>        
26763>>>>>>>>>        //  Get the row from the action data
26763>>>>>>>>>        Get phoActionJsonData to hoJson
26764>>>>>>>>>        Get JsonToDataType of hoJson to aActionData
26765>>>>>>>>>        
26765>>>>>>>>>        If (SizeOfArray(aActionData) > 0) Begin
26767>>>>>>>>>            Move aActionData[0] to tSelectRow
26768>>>>>>>>>            
26768>>>>>>>>>            //  Update rowid
26768>>>>>>>>>            WebSet psCurrentRowId to tSelectRow.sRowID
26769>>>>>>>>>            
26769>>>>>>>>>            //  Update the DEO's (columns)
26769>>>>>>>>>            Get phoColumnObjects to aColumns
26770>>>>>>>>>            For iCol from 0 to (SizeOfArray(aColumns) - 1)
26776>>>>>>>>>>
26776>>>>>>>>>                Get pbIsWebColumn of aColumns[iCol] to bCol
26777>>>>>>>>>                If (bCol) Begin
26779>>>>>>>>>                    Get ConvertFromTransport of aColumns[iCol] (RefFunc(psValue)) tSelectRow.aCells[iCol].sValue cArgStr to sValue
26780>>>>>>>>>                    WebSet psValue of aColumns[iCol] to sValue
26781>>>>>>>>>                    
26781>>>>>>>>>                    WebSet pbChanged of aColumns[iCol] to False
26782>>>>>>>>>                End
26782>>>>>>>>>>
26782>>>>>>>>>            Loop
26783>>>>>>>>>>
26783>>>>>>>>>                            
26783>>>>>>>>>        End
26783>>>>>>>>>>
26783>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
26784>>>>>>>>>            Error DFERR_PROGRAM "Assert: No row data in a action data."
26785>>>>>>>>>>
26785>>>>>>>>>        End
26785>>>>>>>>>>
26785>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
26786>>>>>>>>>    
26786>>>>>>>>>    // Sent by ChangeCurrentRow. User hook to perform processing when when the client navigates the
26786>>>>>>>>>    // focus from one row to another.
26786>>>>>>>>>    Procedure OnChangeCurrentRow String sFromRowID String sToRowID
26788>>>>>>>>>        
26788>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
26789>>>>>>>>>    
26789>>>>>>>>>    
26789>>>>>>>>>    // Alternative name for piOrdering (depreciated). Used for concistency with VDF Windows classes. See also piOrdering
26789>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Ordering Integer iOrdering
26791>>>>>>>>>        Set piOrdering to iOrdering
26792>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
26793>>>>>>>>>    
26793>>>>>>>>>    Function Ordering Returns Integer
26795>>>>>>>>>        Integer iOrdering
26795>>>>>>>>>        Get piOrdering to iOrdering
26796>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iOrdering
26797>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
26798>>>>>>>>>
26798>>>>>>>>>    
26798>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Request_Clear
26800>>>>>>>>>        // Request clear message for clear/clear all.
26800>>>>>>>>>        Integer eSelectedRowOperation
26800>>>>>>>>>        Get ClearSelectedRow to eSelectedRowOperation
26801>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
26802>>>>>>>>>    
26802>>>>>>>>>    
26802>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Request_Delete
26804>>>>>>>>>        // Request delete message for DDO delete.
26804>>>>>>>>>        Integer eSelectedRowOperation
26804>>>>>>>>>        Get DeleteSelectedRow to eSelectedRowOperation
26805>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
26806>>>>>>>>>    
26806>>>>>>>>>    
26806>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Request_Save
26808>>>>>>>>>        // Request save message for DDO save.
26808>>>>>>>>>        Integer eSelectedRowOperation
26808>>>>>>>>>        Get SaveSelectedRow to eSelectedRowOperation
26809>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
26810>>>>>>>>>
26810>>>>>>>>>
26810>>>>>>>>>    // RegisterColumn:
26810>>>>>>>>>    
26810>>>>>>>>>    // Registers a column object in the columns collection.
26810>>>>>>>>>    Procedure RegisterColumn Handle hoColumn
26812>>>>>>>>>        Integer iSize
26812>>>>>>>>>        Handle[] hoColumnObjects
26813>>>>>>>>>        Get phoColumnObjects to hoColumnObjects
26814>>>>>>>>>        Move (SizeOfArray(hoColumnObjects)) to iSize
26815>>>>>>>>>        Move hoColumn to hoColumnObjects[iSize]
26816>>>>>>>>>        Set piColumnId of hoColumn to iSize
26817>>>>>>>>>        Set phoColumnObjects to hoColumnObjects
26818>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
26819>>>>>>>>>    
26819>>>>>>>>>    
26819>>>>>>>>>    // Sent by DDO when there is a clear/find/save/delete.
26819>>>>>>>>>    //
26819>>>>>>>>>    // eMode - Determines the type of DDO operation which generated this refresh message. 
26819>>>>>>>>>    //         It may be one of the following:
26819>>>>>>>>>    //         Mode_Clear:             Used only for DEOs attached to the DDO that was the
26819>>>>>>>>>    //                                 "origin" of a Clear operation, (i.e., the DDO received
26819>>>>>>>>>    //                                 the original Clear message). All other DDOs Send their 
26819>>>>>>>>>    //                                 DEOs the refresh message passing mode_find_or_clear_set.  
26819>>>>>>>>>    //         Mode_Find_or_Clear_Set: Used for DEOs attached to DDOs which have Found and/or cleared records.  
26819>>>>>>>>>    //         Mode_Clear_All:         Used for DEOs attached to any DDO that participated in a clear_all operation.  
26819>>>>>>>>>    //         Mode_Delete:            Used for DEOs attached to any DDO that performed a successful deletion. 
26819>>>>>>>>>    //                                 DDOs that were merely updated as the result of a deletion Use Mode_Find_or_Clear_Set.  
26819>>>>>>>>>    //         Mode_Save:              Used for DEOs attached to any DDO involved in a successful Save operation. 
26819>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Refresh Integer eMode
26821>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMainFile
26821>>>>>>>>>        Integer eDDStatus
26821>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDDO
26821>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bActive bAppSynching bMainFound
26821>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bRowDisplay bInClearGrid bDataAware 
26821>>>>>>>>>        Integer eDBGridType
26821>>>>>>>>>        String sCurrentRowID
26821>>>>>>>>>        RowID riCurrentRowID riID
26821>>>>>>>>>        Integer iCurrentRowIndex
26821>>>>>>>>>        
26821>>>>>>>>>        Get Active_State to bActive
26822>>>>>>>>>        Get AppSynching to bAppSynching
26823>>>>>>>>>        Get pbDataAware to bDataAware
26824>>>>>>>>>        Get peDbGridType to eDBGridType
26825>>>>>>>>>
26825>>>>>>>>>        If (bDataAware and bActive and not(bAppSynching)) Begin
26827>>>>>>>>>            Get ReadingServer to hoDDO                  // hoDDO cannot be 0 otherwise we would never receive Refresh!
26828>>>>>>>>>            Get Main_File of hoDDO to iMainFile
26829>>>>>>>>>        
26829>>>>>>>>>            Get DDRefreshTableStatus iMainFile to eDDStatus
26830>>>>>>>>>            Move (eDDStatus <> ddrtsNone) to bMainFound     // True = a main dd find or constrained child dd find has occurred
26831>>>>>>>>>            Get pbNotifyingExternalDD to bRowDisplay                 // True = we are simply responding to a change of the current row ID on the client
26832>>>>>>>>>            
26832>>>>>>>>>            // Get the current row's row id
26832>>>>>>>>>            WebGet psCurrentRowId to sCurrentRowID
26833>>>>>>>>>            Move (DeserializeRowID(sCurrentRowID)) to riCurrentRowID
26834>>>>>>>>>            WebGet piCurrentRowIndex to iCurrentRowIndex
26835>>>>>>>>>        
26835>>>>>>>>>            // Handle the case where there is no selected row and we've done a save or delete on the main file.
26835>>>>>>>>>            // We don't know what to do in this case so we will refresh the grid. This could happen if the save
26835>>>>>>>>>            // is occuring from an external source (e.g., create a new record directly in the DD)
26835>>>>>>>>>            If (iCurrentRowIndex=-1 and (eMode = MODE_SAVE or eMode = MODE_DELETE) and bMainFound and (not(bRowDisplay))) Begin
26837>>>>>>>>>                Move MODE_FIND_OR_CLEAR_SET to eMode
26838>>>>>>>>>            End
26838>>>>>>>>>>
26838>>>>>>>>>
26838>>>>>>>>>            // If this is a clear on the grid's main file and it is not grid insert/append row, all we can do is clear and refresh the grid
26838>>>>>>>>>            Get pbInClearGrid to bInClearGrid
26839>>>>>>>>>            If (bInClearGrid) Begin
26841>>>>>>>>>                Move MODE_FIND_OR_CLEAR_SET to eMode
26842>>>>>>>>>            End
26842>>>>>>>>>>
26842>>>>>>>>>
26842>>>>>>>>>            If (eMode = MODE_CLEAR and bMainFound and sCurrentRowID <> "") Begin
26844>>>>>>>>>                //  HW: Added check for empty current row id which prevents recursive clearing with two grids on a single DD.
26844>>>>>>>>>                // special case with clear. If this comes from some other DEO (which is unusual)
26844>>>>>>>>>                // and the curent row has a record, then we need to insert a row for the
26844>>>>>>>>>                // cleared row.
26844>>>>>>>>>                If (not(bRowDisplay)) Begin
26846>>>>>>>>>                    Send AppendNewRow
26847>>>>>>>>>                End
26847>>>>>>>>>>
26847>>>>>>>>>                
26847>>>>>>>>>                Send UpdateCurrentRowID
26848>>>>>>>>>            End
26848>>>>>>>>>>
26848>>>>>>>>>            
26848>>>>>>>>>            Else If (eMode = MODE_DELETE or eMode = MODE_SAVE or bRowDisplay or not(bMainFound)) Begin
26851>>>>>>>>>                // Perform necessary actions for Save or Delete of a Grid Row
26851>>>>>>>>>                If (hoDDO = OPERATION_ORIGIN) Begin    // OPERATION_ORIGIN is the DDO that is the origin of the Save, Delete, find or clear
26853>>>>>>>>>                    // if a save notification and the save's DD is the same as the grid's
26853>>>>>>>>>                    // we are saving the main record and it may now be out of order
26853>>>>>>>>>                    If (eMode = MODE_SAVE) Begin
26855>>>>>>>>>                        WebSet pbUnOrdered to True
26856>>>>>>>>>                    End
26856>>>>>>>>>>
26856>>>>>>>>>                End
26856>>>>>>>>>>
26856>>>>>>>>>
26856>>>>>>>>>                Send UpdateCurrentRowID
26857>>>>>>>>>            End
26857>>>>>>>>>>
26857>>>>>>>>>            
26857>>>>>>>>>            Else If (eMode = MODE_CLEAR_ALL) Begin
26860>>>>>>>>>                Send UpdateCurrentRowID
26861>>>>>>>>>                If (eDBGridType<>gtManual) Begin
26863>>>>>>>>>                    Send EmptyGridRefresh
26864>>>>>>>>>                    Set psFilter to ""
26865>>>>>>>>>                End
26865>>>>>>>>>>
26865>>>>>>>>>            End
26865>>>>>>>>>>
26865>>>>>>>>>            Else If (eMode = MODE_FIND_OR_CLEAR_SET) Begin
26868>>>>>>>>>                // If we got here then refresh the entire grid
26868>>>>>>>>>                Move (GetRowID(iMainFile)) to riID
26869>>>>>>>>>                Send UpdateCurrentRowID
26870>>>>>>>>>                If (eDBGridType<>gtManual) Begin
26872>>>>>>>>>                    Send GridRefresh
26873>>>>>>>>>                End
26873>>>>>>>>>>
26873>>>>>>>>>                Send ReadByRowId of hoDDO iMainFile riID
26874>>>>>>>>>            End
26874>>>>>>>>>>
26874>>>>>>>>>        End
26874>>>>>>>>>>
26874>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
26875>>>>>>>>>    
26875>>>>>>>>>    
26875>>>>>>>>>    // Does nothing in cWebList. See ClearSelectedRow in cWebGrid class.
26875>>>>>>>>>    // returns True.
26875>>>>>>>>>    Function ClearSelectedRow Returns Boolean
26877>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return True
26878>>>>>>>>>    End_Function  
26879>>>>>>>>>    
26879>>>>>>>>>    // Does nothing in cWebList. cWebList is read only. See SaveSelectedRow in cWebGrid class.
26879>>>>>>>>>    Function SaveSelectedRow Returns Integer
26881>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return sroSucceed
26882>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
26883>>>>>>>>>    
26883>>>>>>>>>    // Delete Logic to delete the current row pointed to by psCurrentRowId.
26883>>>>>>>>>    // returns True if the delete was successful.
26883>>>>>>>>>    Function DeleteSelectedRow Returns Integer
26885>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDD
26885>>>>>>>>>        Handle hmVerify
26885>>>>>>>>>        RowID riCurrentRowID riTestRowID
26885>>>>>>>>>        String sCurrentRowID
26885>>>>>>>>>        Integer iOrdering iMainFile
26885>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bReverseOrdering
26885>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bDataAware
26885>>>>>>>>>        Integer iReturn
26885>>>>>>>>>
26885>>>>>>>>>        WebGet psCurrentRowId to sCurrentRowID
26886>>>>>>>>>        Get pbDataAware to bDataAware
26887>>>>>>>>>        
26887>>>>>>>>>        // db-aware handling
26887>>>>>>>>>        If (bDataAware) Begin
26889>>>>>>>>>            Get Server to hoDD
26890>>>>>>>>>            If (hoDD <> 0) Begin
26892>>>>>>>>>                Move (DeserializeRowID(sCurrentRowID)) to riCurrentRowID
26893>>>>>>>>>                Get CurrentRowId of hoDD to riTestRowID
26894>>>>>>>>>                
26894>>>>>>>>>                If (not(IsSameRowID(riCurrentRowID, riTestRowID))) Begin
26896>>>>>>>>>                    Error DFERR_PROGRAM "Assert: Server DDO's current record does not match psCurrentRowId"
26897>>>>>>>>>>
26897>>>>>>>>>                    Function_Return sroFail
26898>>>>>>>>>                End
26898>>>>>>>>>>
26898>>>>>>>>>                
26898>>>>>>>>>                // Verify that we are allowed to delete
26898>>>>>>>>>                If (Read_Only_State(hoDD) or not(pbAllowDeleteRow(Self)) or not(Can_Delete(hoDD))) Begin
26900>>>>>>>>>                    Function_Return sroFail         // the view should not allow this to happen
26901>>>>>>>>>                End
26901>>>>>>>>>>
26901>>>>>>>>>            End
26901>>>>>>>>>>
26901>>>>>>>>>        End
26901>>>>>>>>>>
26901>>>>>>>>>        
26901>>>>>>>>>        Get Verify_Delete_msg to hmVerify
26902>>>>>>>>>        If (hmVerify) Begin
26904>>>>>>>>>            WebSet pbDeleteCallbackActive to True
26905>>>>>>>>>            Send VerifyRequest (RefProc(RequestDeleteCallBack)) (RefFunc(Verify_Delete_Msg))
26906>>>>>>>>>            Function_Return sroPending
26907>>>>>>>>>        End
26907>>>>>>>>>>
26907>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
26908>>>>>>>>>            Send RequestDeleteExec
26909>>>>>>>>>            // we actually don't know if this will work or not, since this finds another row. For now, we say success
26909>>>>>>>>>        End
26909>>>>>>>>>>
26909>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return sroSucceed
26910>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
26911>>>>>>>>>    
26911>>>>>>>>>    // This event is triggered by Request_Delete. It is intended to be implemented on grids having 
26911>>>>>>>>>    // pbDataAware set to false to process the delete. If the delete cannot be performed return 
26911>>>>>>>>>    // false to cancel the grid from removing the row from the display. Returning false when 
26911>>>>>>>>>    // pbDataAware is set to true will also cancel the delete from being sent to the DDO.
26911>>>>>>>>>    Function OnDeleteRow String sCurrentRowID Returns Boolean
26913>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return True
26914>>>>>>>>>    End_Function        
26915>>>>>>>>>
26915>>>>>>>>>    
26915>>>>>>>>>    Procedure RequestDeleteExec
26917>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDD
26917>>>>>>>>>        String sCurrentRowID
26917>>>>>>>>>        Integer iOrdering iMainFile
26917>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bReverseOrdering
26917>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bDataAware bContinue
26917>>>>>>>>>
26917>>>>>>>>>        WebGet psCurrentRowId to sCurrentRowID
26918>>>>>>>>>        Get OnDeleteRow sCurrentRowID to bContinue
26919>>>>>>>>>        
26919>>>>>>>>>        // db-aware
26919>>>>>>>>>        Get pbDataAware to bDataAware
26920>>>>>>>>>        
26920>>>>>>>>>        If (bDataAware) Begin
26922>>>>>>>>>            If (bContinue) Begin
26924>>>>>>>>>                // Perform the db-aware delete
26924>>>>>>>>>                Get Server to hoDD
26925>>>>>>>>>                Send Request_Delete to hoDD       // Perform the delete
26926>>>>>>>>>                            
26926>>>>>>>>>                If (Err) Begin
26928>>>>>>>>>                    Procedure_Return
26929>>>>>>>>>                End
26929>>>>>>>>>>
26929>>>>>>>>>                
26929>>>>>>>>>                Send RemoveRow sCurrentRowID      // Tell the client to remove the deleted row.
26930>>>>>>>>>                
26930>>>>>>>>>                // Select the next logical row
26930>>>>>>>>>                Get IndexOrder to iOrdering
26931>>>>>>>>>                WebGet pbReverseOrdering to bReverseOrdering
26932>>>>>>>>>                Get Main_File of hoDD to iMainFile
26933>>>>>>>>>        
26933>>>>>>>>>                If (bReverseOrdering) Begin
26935>>>>>>>>>                    Send Establish_Find_Direction of hoDD LT iMainFile iOrdering 
26936>>>>>>>>>                End
26936>>>>>>>>>>
26936>>>>>>>>>                Else Begin
26937>>>>>>>>>                    Send Establish_Find_Direction of hoDD GT iMainFile iOrdering 
26938>>>>>>>>>                End
26938>>>>>>>>>>
26938>>>>>>>>>                
26938>>>>>>>>>                Send Locate_Next of hoDD    // Try to find the row below the deleted row.
26939>>>>>>>>>                
26939>>>>>>>>>                If (not(Found)) Begin
26941>>>>>>>>>                    // If the row below the deleted row was not found then it means we deleted the
26941>>>>>>>>>                    // last row. Now we will try to load the new last row. If there are no remaining
26941>>>>>>>>>                    // rows in the dataset then the buffer will be automatically cleared (which is 
26941>>>>>>>>>                    // what we want)
26941>>>>>>>>>                    If (bReverseOrdering) Begin
26943>>>>>>>>>                        Send Request_Read of hoDD FIRST_RECORD iMainFile iOrdering
26944>>>>>>>>>                    End
26944>>>>>>>>>>
26944>>>>>>>>>                    Else Begin
26945>>>>>>>>>                        Send Request_Read of hoDD LAST_RECORD iMainFile iOrdering
26946>>>>>>>>>                    End
26946>>>>>>>>>>
26946>>>>>>>>>                End
26946>>>>>>>>>>
26946>>>>>>>>>                
26946>>>>>>>>>                If (Found) Begin
26948>>>>>>>>>                    Send Request_Assign of hoDD iMainFile
26949>>>>>>>>>                End
26949>>>>>>>>>>
26949>>>>>>>>>                Else Begin
26950>>>>>>>>>                    Send ClearGrid
26951>>>>>>>>>                End
26951>>>>>>>>>>
26951>>>>>>>>>                
26951>>>>>>>>>                Send UpdateCurrentRowID
26952>>>>>>>>>            End
26952>>>>>>>>>>
26952>>>>>>>>>        End 
26952>>>>>>>>>>
26952>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
26953>>>>>>>>>            //  Non DB-Aware handling
26953>>>>>>>>>             If (bContinue) Begin
26955>>>>>>>>>                Send RemoveRow sCurrentRowID      // Tell the client to remove the deleted row.
26956>>>>>>>>>            End
26956>>>>>>>>>>
26956>>>>>>>>>        End
26956>>>>>>>>>>
26956>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
26957>>>>>>>>>    
26957>>>>>>>>>    // Client action to remove the passed row from the cache. 
26957>>>>>>>>>    Procedure RemoveRow String sRowID
26959>>>>>>>>>        String[] aParams
26960>>>>>>>>>        
26960>>>>>>>>>        Move sRowID to aParams[0]
26961>>>>>>>>>        Send ClientAction "removeRow" aParams    
26962>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
26963>>>>>>>>>
26963>>>>>>>>>    // Returns true if you can move off of the selected row.
26963>>>>>>>>>    // Does nothing in cWebList. cWebList is read only. See AllowChangeSelectedRow in cWebGrid class.
26963>>>>>>>>>    Function AllowChangeSelectedRow String sGotoRow String sToRowID Returns Boolean
26965>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return True
26966>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
26967>>>>>>>>>
26967>>>>>>>>>    // these don't do anything with lists
26967>>>>>>>>>    Procedure AppendNewRow    
26969>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
26970>>>>>>>>>
26970>>>>>>>>>    // these don't do anything with lists
26970>>>>>>>>>    Procedure InsertNewRow    
26972>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
26973>>>>>>>>>    
26973>>>>>>>>>    Function IndexOrder Returns Integer
26975>>>>>>>>>        // returns the sort order for subsequent DDO Request_Read calls.
26975>>>>>>>>>        Integer iOrdering iColumnOrdering eDbGridType iConstrainFile
26975>>>>>>>>>        String iSortColumn
26975>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoColumn hoDD
26975>>>>>>>>>        
26975>>>>>>>>>        
26975>>>>>>>>>        
26975>>>>>>>>>        // if DD has an ordering we must use this
26975>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoDD
26976>>>>>>>>>        If (hoDD > 0) Begin
26978>>>>>>>>>            Get Ordering of hoDD to iOrdering    // get the sort index from the DDO (if this has been set)
26979>>>>>>>>>            If (iOrdering<>-1) Begin
26981>>>>>>>>>                Function_Return iOrdering
26982>>>>>>>>>            End
26982>>>>>>>>>>
26982>>>>>>>>>        End
26982>>>>>>>>>>
26982>>>>>>>>>            
26982>>>>>>>>>        Get piOrdering to iOrdering
26983>>>>>>>>>        If (hoDD > 0) Begin
26985>>>>>>>>>            // this is the ordering as defined by the grid
26985>>>>>>>>>            Get Constrain_File of hoDD to iConstrainFile
26986>>>>>>>>>            // if ordering is not specified and we have a constraining parent
26986>>>>>>>>>            // we want to limit the constraint to the best choice for a constrained find
26986>>>>>>>>>            If (iOrdering=-1 and iConstrainFile) Begin
26988>>>>>>>>>                Get ConstrainedIndexOrder iConstrainFile to iOrdering
26989>>>>>>>>>            End
26989>>>>>>>>>>
26989>>>>>>>>>        End
26989>>>>>>>>>>
26989>>>>>>>>>        // if a static grid, use the grid's ordering, if dynamic we use
26989>>>>>>>>>        // the column ordering if we are sorting by a grid column, else use grid ordering
26989>>>>>>>>>        Get peDbGridType to eDbGridType
26990>>>>>>>>>        If (eDbGridType=gtAutomatic) Begin
26992>>>>>>>>>            // If we are sorting by a grid column then use that
26992>>>>>>>>>            WebGet piSortColumn to iSortColumn
26993>>>>>>>>>            
26993>>>>>>>>>            If (iSortColumn <> -1) Begin
26995>>>>>>>>>                Get GetColumnObject iSortColumn to hoColumn
26996>>>>>>>>>                If (hoColumn) Begin
26998>>>>>>>>>                    Get ColumnIndexOrder of hoColumn to iColumnOrdering      // returns -1 if there is no default index
26999>>>>>>>>>                    If (iColumnOrdering<>-1) Begin
27001>>>>>>>>>                        Move iColumnOrdering to iOrdering
27002>>>>>>>>>                    End
27002>>>>>>>>>>
27002>>>>>>>>>                End
27002>>>>>>>>>>
27002>>>>>>>>>            End
27002>>>>>>>>>>
27002>>>>>>>>>        End
27002>>>>>>>>>>
27002>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iOrdering
27003>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
27004>>>>>>>>>    
27004>>>>>>>>>    
27004>>>>>>>>>    // return best index for constrained find. Return -1 which asks the runtime
27004>>>>>>>>>    // to make this choice as normally there is only one choice. 
27004>>>>>>>>>    // This is suitable for augmentation.
27004>>>>>>>>>    Function ConstrainedIndexOrder Integer iConstrainFile Returns Integer
27006>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return -1 // the runtime knows best
27007>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
27008>>>>>>>>>    
27008>>>>>>>>>    
27008>>>>>>>>>    Procedure UpdateCurrentRowID
27010>>>>>>>>>        // Sets the web property psCurrentRowId for pbDataAware=True grid.
27010>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDD
27010>>>>>>>>>        RowID riRowID
27010>>>>>>>>>        
27010>>>>>>>>>        // assert pbDataAware=True
27010>>>>>>>>>        If (not(pbDataAware(Self))) Begin
27012>>>>>>>>>            Error DFERR_PROGRAM "Assert: UpdateCurrentRowID called for non-data aware grid"
27013>>>>>>>>>>
27013>>>>>>>>>        End
27013>>>>>>>>>>
27013>>>>>>>>>        
27013>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoDD
27014>>>>>>>>>        
27014>>>>>>>>>        If (hoDD = 0) Begin
27016>>>>>>>>>            // This will probably never happen
27016>>>>>>>>>            Move (NullRowID()) to riRowID
27017>>>>>>>>>        End
27017>>>>>>>>>>
27017>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
27018>>>>>>>>>            Get CurrentRowId of hoDD to riRowID
27019>>>>>>>>>        End
27019>>>>>>>>>>
27019>>>>>>>>>        
27019>>>>>>>>>        WebSet psCurrentRowId to (SerializeRowID(riRowID))
27020>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
27021>>>>>>>>>
27021>>>>>>>>>
27021>>>>>>>>>    // in sub-classes that support auto-server, which uses the
27021>>>>>>>>>    // invoking server, the server used for reading the grid may
27021>>>>>>>>>    // be different than the server defined in this view.
27021>>>>>>>>>    Function ReadingServer Returns Handle
27023>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDD
27023>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoDD
27024>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return hoDD
27025>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
27026>>>>>>>>>
27026>>>>>>>>>    // This handles translation of find modes to make reverse ordering
27026>>>>>>>>>    // work. Pass the mode and return the mode, translated if reverse ordering is needed
27026>>>>>>>>>    Function FindMode Integer eFindMode Boolean bReverseOrdering Returns Integer
27028>>>>>>>>>        If (bReverseOrdering) Begin
27030>>>>>>>>>            Case Begin
27030>>>>>>>>>                Case (eFindMode=GE) ;                    Move (LE) to eFindMode
27033>>>>>>>>>                Case (eFindMode=GT) ;                    Move (LT) to eFindMode
27037>>>>>>>>>                Case (eFindMode=LT) ;                    Move (GT) to eFindMode
27041>>>>>>>>>                Case (eFindMode=LE) ;                    Move (GE) to eFindMode
27045>>>>>>>>>                Case (eFindMode=FIRST_RECORD) ;                    Move (LAST_RECORD) to eFindMode
27049>>>>>>>>>                Case (eFindMode=LAST_RECORD) ;                    Move (FIRST_RECORD) to eFindMode
27053>>>>>>>>>            Case End
27053>>>>>>>>>        End
27053>>>>>>>>>>
27053>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return eFindMode
27054>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
27055>>>>>>>>>
27055>>>>>>>>>    Procedure EstablishDDFindMode Integer eFindMode Handle hoServer Integer iOrdering Boolean bReverseOrdering
27057>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
27057>>>>>>>>>        Get FindMode eFindMode bReverseOrdering to eFindMode  // mode might change if reverse ordering
27058>>>>>>>>>        Get Main_File of hoServer to iFile
27059>>>>>>>>>        Send Establish_Find_Direction of hoServer eFindMode iFile iOrdering
27060>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
27061>>>>>>>>>
27061>>>>>>>>>    Function ReadDDFirstRecord Handle hoDD Integer iOrdering Boolean bReverseOrdering  Returns RowID
27063>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile eFindMode
27063>>>>>>>>>        // because this uses request_read it cannot be used inside of refresh
27063>>>>>>>>>        If (OPERATION_MODE<>0) Begin
27065>>>>>>>>>            Error DFERR_PROGRAM ("assertion failed: ReadDDFirstRecord is called when DD is busy")
27066>>>>>>>>>>
27066>>>>>>>>>        End
27066>>>>>>>>>>
27066>>>>>>>>>        Get Main_File of hoDD to iFile
27067>>>>>>>>>        Get FindMode FIRST_RECORD bReverseOrdering to eFindMode
27068>>>>>>>>>        Send Request_Read of hoDD eFindMode iFile  iOrdering
27069>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (GetRowID(iFile))
27070>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
27071>>>>>>>>>    
27071>>>>>>>>>    
27071>>>>>>>>>    Function ReadDDLastRecord Handle hoDD Integer iOrdering Boolean bReverseOrdering  Returns RowID
27073>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile eFindMode
27073>>>>>>>>>        // because this uses request_read it cannot be used inside of refresh
27073>>>>>>>>>        If (OPERATION_MODE<>0) Begin
27075>>>>>>>>>            Error DFERR_PROGRAM ("assertion failed: ReadDDFirstRecord is called when DD is busy")
27076>>>>>>>>>>
27076>>>>>>>>>        End
27076>>>>>>>>>>
27076>>>>>>>>>        Get Main_File of hoDD to iFile
27077>>>>>>>>>        Get FindMode LAST_RECORD bReverseOrdering to eFindMode
27078>>>>>>>>>        Send Request_Read of hoDD eFindMode iFile iOrdering
27079>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (GetRowID(iFile))
27080>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
27081>>>>>>>>>    
27081>>>>>>>>>    Function ReadDDRecordInBuffer Handle hoDD Integer iOrdering Boolean bReverseOrdering Returns Boolean
27083>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bFound
27083>>>>>>>>>        RowID riId
27083>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
27083>>>>>>>>>        
27083>>>>>>>>>        Send EstablishDDFindMode Ge  hoDD iOrdering bReverseOrdering
27084>>>>>>>>>        Send Locate_Next of hoDD
27085>>>>>>>>>        Move (Found) to bFound
27086>>>>>>>>>        If not bFound Begin
27088>>>>>>>>>            Get ReadDDLastRecord hoDD iOrdering bReverseOrdering to riId
27089>>>>>>>>>        End
27089>>>>>>>>>>
27089>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
27090>>>>>>>>>            Get Main_File of hoDD to iFile
27091>>>>>>>>>            Move (GetRowID(iFile)) to riId
27092>>>>>>>>>        End
27092>>>>>>>>>>
27092>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (not(IsNullRowID(riId)))
27093>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
27094>>>>>>>>>
27094>>>>>>>>>    // finds the record in the buffer and rebuilds the list. If the
27094>>>>>>>>>    // buffer record is not found, most likely due to a failed constraint), it
27094>>>>>>>>>    // search for the next record (where next is determined by reverse ordering).
27094>>>>>>>>>    // If there is no record, it will attemot to find the prior record. 
27094>>>>>>>>>    Procedure FindDDRecordInBuffer 
27096>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bReverseOrdering bFound
27096>>>>>>>>>        Integer iOrdering
27096>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDD
27096>>>>>>>>>
27096>>>>>>>>>        Get ReadingServer to hoDD
27097>>>>>>>>>        Get IndexOrder to iOrdering
27098>>>>>>>>>        WebGet pbReverseOrdering to bReverseOrdering
27099>>>>>>>>>        
27099>>>>>>>>>        Get ReadDDRecordInBuffer hoDD iOrdering bReverseOrdering to bFound
27100>>>>>>>>>        
27100>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoDD
27101>>>>>>>>>        If bFound Begin
27103>>>>>>>>>            Send Request_Assign of hoDD
27104>>>>>>>>>        End
27104>>>>>>>>>>
27104>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
27105>>>>>>>>>            Send ClearGrid
27106>>>>>>>>>        End
27106>>>>>>>>>>
27106>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
27107>>>>>>>>>    
27107>>>>>>>>>    
27107>>>>>>>>>    // Clears the DD and creates an empty grid.
27107>>>>>>>>>    // The Clear DD behavior can work different ways with grids. Most of the time, a clear to a DD should
27107>>>>>>>>>    // just open up a new row for editing. This is consistent with what clear does everyhwere else. However, there are
27107>>>>>>>>>    // times when you need to create an empty grid. This will mostly happen when there are no valid records to display so you
27107>>>>>>>>>    // need to create an empty grid. That's what this message is for.
27107>>>>>>>>>    // For now this is public, but it needs to be used carefully. If you are clearing grids when there are records that could be
27107>>>>>>>>>    // displayed, you are fighting a normal grid behavior.
27107>>>>>>>>>    Procedure ClearGrid
27109>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bInClearGrid bDataAware
27109>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDD
27109>>>>>>>>>        
27109>>>>>>>>>        Get pbDataAware to bDataAware
27110>>>>>>>>>        
27110>>>>>>>>>        If (bDataAware) Begin
27112>>>>>>>>>            Get pbInClearGrid to bInClearGrid
27113>>>>>>>>>            Set pbInClearGrid to True
27114>>>>>>>>>            Get Server to hoDD
27115>>>>>>>>>            Send Clear of hoDD
27116>>>>>>>>>            Set pbInClearGrid to bInClearGrid
27117>>>>>>>>>        End
27117>>>>>>>>>>
27117>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
27118>>>>>>>>>            Send EmptyGridRefresh
27119>>>>>>>>>        End
27119>>>>>>>>>>
27119>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
27120>>>>>>>>>    
27120>>>>>>>>>    
27120>>>>>>>>>    // Appends a row to the end of the list. It will update the user interface if needed. Should
27120>>>>>>>>>    // only be used on a manually loaded list (pbDataAware = false or peDbGridType = gtManual). 
27120>>>>>>>>>    // Implemented as a client-action meaning that it works asynchronously.
27120>>>>>>>>>    //
27120>>>>>>>>>    // Params:
27120>>>>>>>>>    //  tRow    Filled tWebRow struct with the new row data.
27120>>>>>>>>>    Procedure DataSetAppendRow tWebRow tRow
27122>>>>>>>>>        String[] aParams
27123>>>>>>>>>        tWebRow[] aRows
27123>>>>>>>>>        tWebRow[] aRows
27124>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoJson
27124>>>>>>>>>        
27124>>>>>>>>>        Move tRow to aRows[0]
27125>>>>>>>>>        
27125>>>>>>>>>        //  Convert data to JSON
27125>>>>>>>>>        Get Create (RefClass(cJsonObject)) to hoJson
27126>>>>>>>>>        Send DataTypeToJson of hoJson aRows
27127>>>>>>>>>        
27127>>>>>>>>>        Send ClientActionEx "dataSetAppendRow" aParams hoJson
27128>>>>>>>>>        Send Destroy of hoJson
27129>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
