29458>>>>>>>>>>>    //  Searches for a token in the current chunk starting at the current position (iChunkRead). It
29458>>>>>>>>>>>    //  will peek in the next chunk if the token starts in the current chunk and continues into the
29458>>>>>>>>>>>    //  next chunk. It will not search the next chunk. 
29458>>>>>>>>>>>    //
29458>>>>>>>>>>>    //  Params:
29458>>>>>>>>>>>    //      parseData   Parsing data.
29458>>>>>>>>>>>    //      ucToken     Token to find in the current chunk data.
29458>>>>>>>>>>>    //      bSkip       If true it will move the current position (iChunkRead) past the found token.
29458>>>>>>>>>>>    //      bBoundary   If true it will not search past the next boundary (iBoundPos).
29458>>>>>>>>>>>    //  Returns:
29458>>>>>>>>>>>    //      The start position of the token, -1 if the token is not found in the current chunk.
29458>>>>>>>>>>>    Function FindToken tMultipartParsingData ByRef parsedata UChar[] ucToken Boolean bSkip Boolean bBoundary Returns Integer
29460>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iTokenPos iSplit iRead
29460>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bEqual
29460>>>>>>>>>>>        
29460>>>>>>>>>>>        //  If we are already at the split then we move to the next chunk (we don't want to miss out out on tokens starting on the split)
29460>>>>>>>>>>>        If (bSkip and parsedata.iChunkRead >= SizeOfArray(parsedata.ucCurrentChunk)) Begin
29462>>>>>>>>>>>            Send ReadChunk (&parsedata)
29463>>>>>>>>>>>        End
29463>>>>>>>>>>>>
29463>>>>>>>>>>>        
29463>>>>>>>>>>>        Move parsedata.iChunkRead to iRead
