39599>>>    // Add code to customize your Zoom View based on how it was invoked.
39599>>>    // Use NavigateData to determine the context this view will be used in.
39599>>>    Procedure OnNavigateForward tWebNavigateData NavigateData Integer hoInvokingView Integer hoInvokingObject
39602>>>
39602>>>        // if this view is being used in multiple contexts, you may need a block of code
39602>>>        // like this to handle customizations. This would include hiding rows and buttons
39602>>>        // (WebSet pbRender) and changing the values of various captions.
39602>>>        Case Begin
39602>>>            Case (NavigateData.eNavigateType = nfFromMain)
39604>>>                // If from main, this is a probably a main file Select to Zoom.
39604>>>                // This is the most typical way to navigate to a zoom.
39604>>>                Case Break
39605>>>                
39605>>>            Case (NavigateData.eNavigateType = nfFromParent)
39608>>>                // If from parent, this is a constrained drill down.
39608>>>                // If needed, you could check NavigateData.iTable to determine the constraining parent.
39608>>>                // This would be unusual - normally you drill down from a parent to a list (Select view).
39608>>>                Case Break
39609>>>                
39609>>>            Case (NavigateData.eNavigateType = nfFromChild)
39612>>>                // If from child, this is a probably a parent Zoom from a Zoom. 
39612>>>                // This is unusual, but it might be used for adding a new child record.
39612>>>                Case Break
39613>>>                
39613>>>            Case Else // must be nfUndefined
39613>>>                // This may be the start of a query or this may be used for some kind of custom operation.
39613>>>                // You may want to check NavigateData.NamedValues.
39613>>>                  
39613>>>        Case End
39613>>>
39613>>>        // Action buttons can be changed dynamically during a Zoom's display lifetime.
39613>>>        // It's best to set these buttons in their own procedure so you can change later.
39613>>>        Send SetActionButtons
39614>>>
39614>>>    End_Procedure
